D("penal",{etymology:E("From Old French peinal and Medieval Latin penalis, from Latin poenalis ‘pertaining to punishment’ and poena ‘punishment’.",null,"poena","-al","Etymonline, penal (https://www.etymonline.com/word/penal)."),contexts:[C("penal.s1","法律","The report compared penal codes to see how each jurisdiction punished repeat fraud.","報告比較各地的刑事法典，了解各司法管轄區如何處罰重複詐欺。","Penal means connected with punishment by law, especially imprisonment.","Attributive adjective before codes; to see states the report’s purpose.","These codes set legal punishments for offenses.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The penal code described only recipes and gardening advice, with no laws or punishments in it.","The gardening handbook described recipes and planting advice, not a penal code.","A penal code concerns legal offenses and punishment; recipes and gardening advice are outside its subject.")],quiz:[Q("penal.q1","penal.s1","meaning","A penal system deals with ___.",["punishment under law","the design of writing tools","animal breeding"],"punishment under law","Penal is the adjective relating to legal punishment.","meaning"),Q("penal.q2","penal.s1","context","Which document is penal?",["A statute setting prison terms for fraud","A guide to planting tulips","A manual for repairing pens"],"A statute setting prison terms for fraud","It prescribes punishment for legal offenses.","context"),Q("penal.q3","penal.s1","grammar","Choose the adjective: “The court reviewed the ____ code.”",["penal","penalty","penalize"],"penal","The blank modifies code and requires an adjective.","grammar"),Q("penal.q4","penal.s1","word-choice","The case involved a ____ sanction imposed by law.",["penal","pendulous","pensive"],"penal","A sanction imposed by law is penal.","word-choice")]});
D("penalize",{etymology:E("Formed from penal + -ize; the verb was first used in sports for disadvantaging a competitor after a rule breach and later for imposing legal punishment.",null,"penal","-ize","Etymonline, penalize (https://www.etymonline.com/word/penalize)."),contexts:[C("penalize.s1","法律","The rule may penalize a contractor who knowingly submits false safety records.","明知故犯提交虛假安全紀錄的承包商可能會受到規則處罰。","Penalize means punish someone or put them at a disadvantage.","May penalize is followed by the person affected; who introduces the offense.","The sanction follows a deliberate breach of the rule.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The referee penalized the player by awarding her team an extra point for breaking the rules.","The referee rewarded the player by awarding her team an extra point for breaking the rules.","A penalty disadvantages or punishes a rule-breaker; awarding an extra point is a reward.")],quiz:[Q("penalize.q1","penalize.s1","meaning","To penalize a competitor is to ___.",["punish or disadvantage them for a breach","give them an advantage for no reason","record their name without action"],"punish or disadvantage them for a breach","The verb describes imposing a consequence or disadvantage.","meaning"),Q("penalize.q2","penalize.s1","context","Which action penalizes a late applicant?",["The office applies the stated late fee.","The office waives every fee and grants extra time.","The office files the form without reviewing it."],"The office applies the stated late fee.","The fee is a consequence of missing the deadline.","context"),Q("penalize.q3","penalize.s1","verb-form","Choose the past form: “The league ____ the club for breaking the rule.”",["penalized","penalize","penalizing"],"penalized","The regular past tense adds -d after final e.","verb-form"),Q("penalize.q4","penalize.s1","word-choice","The new policy should not ____ workers who report hazards honestly.",["penalize","pendulum","perceive"],"penalize","The sentence means workers should not be punished or disadvantaged.","word-choice")]});
D("penalty",{etymology:E("From Old French penalite and Medieval Latin penalitas, based on Latin poenalis ‘pertaining to punishment’; sports later used it for a disadvantage imposed after a rule breach.",null,"poenalis","-ty","Etymonline, penalty (https://www.etymonline.com/word/penalty)."),contexts:[C("penalty.s1","法律","The contract states a penalty for disclosing confidential plans before the launch date.","合約規定，若在上市日期前洩露機密計畫，將受到處罰。","A penalty is punishment for breaking a law, rule, or contract.","A penalty for disclosing names the violation; before sets the deadline.","The contract specifies a consequence for breaching confidentiality."),C("penalty.s2","体育","The referee awarded a penalty after the defender handled the ball inside the box.","防守球員在禁區內手球後，裁判判給對方一次罰球。","In sport, a penalty is a chance to score given because the other team broke a rule.","Awarded a penalty after identifies the decision and its cause.","The defender’s foul gives the opposing team a scoring opportunity."),C("penalty.s3","通用","One penalty of taking the mountain route is that deliveries arrive a day later.","走山路的一項不利後果，是貨物會晚一天送達。","A penalty can be a disadvantage that follows from a situation or action.","One penalty of introduces a drawback; that clause states it.","The route has a practical cost in delivery time.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The referee awarded a penalty to the defending team after its opponent committed a foul, giving the defending team no disadvantage or consequence.","The referee awarded a penalty to the fouled team after its opponent committed a foul.","A sports penalty is awarded because a rule was broken; it is not normally a reward for the offending side.")],quiz:[Q("penalty.q1","penalty.s1","meaning","A contractual penalty is ___.",["a consequence for breaking an agreement","a prize for signing early","a copy of the contract"],"a consequence for breaking an agreement","This sense is punishment for violating a contract or rule.","meaning"),Q("penalty.q2","penalty.s2","context","Why might a soccer referee award a penalty?",["A defender commits a foul inside the penalty area.","A goalkeeper catches a legal shot.","A player passes the ball to a teammate."],"A defender commits a foul inside the penalty area.","The foul triggers a scoring chance for the other team.","context"),Q("penalty.q3","penalty.s3","meaning","A penalty of living far from town might be ___.",["a longer trip to the grocery store","a free grocery delivery every day","a shorter commute to every shop"],"a longer trip to the grocery store","Here penalty means a drawback or disadvantage.","meaning"),Q("penalty.q4","penalty.s2","word-choice","The foul inside the box resulted in a ____ kick.",["penalty","pencil","pendant"],"penalty","A penalty kick follows a qualifying foul.","word-choice")]});
D("pence",{etymology:E("A contraction of Middle English penies, the collective plural of penny; its -ce spelling reflects the voiceless final pronunciation.",null,"penny",null,"Etymonline, pence (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pence)."),contexts:[C("pence.s1","金融","The shop raised the price by twenty pence after the supplier increased its delivery charge.","供應商提高運費後，商店把價格調漲了二十便士。","Pence is the plural currency unit of penny in Britain.","By twenty pence states the amount of the increase; after gives its cause.","The price changes by twenty one-hundredths of a pound.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The cashier returned fifty pence in change, meaning fifty British pounds in notes.","The cashier returned fifty pounds in change, meaning fifty British pounds in notes.","Pence are subdivisions of a pound, not whole pounds; fifty pence is less than one pound.")],quiz:[Q("pence.q1","pence.s1","meaning","One hundred pence make ___.",["one British pound","one hundred pounds","one euro exactly"],"one British pound","The British pound is divided into 100 pence.","meaning"),Q("pence.q2","pence.s1","context","Which amount is written in pence?",["35p","£35","35 dollars"],"35p","The p after the number denotes pence.","context"),Q("pence.q3","pence.s1","plural","Choose the British plural currency form: “The ticket costs eighty ____.”",["pence","pennieses","penny's"],"pence","Pence is the standard plural unit for British money.","plural"),Q("pence.q4","pence.s1","meaning","A coin marked 20p is worth ___.",["twenty pence","twenty pounds","two hundred pence"],"twenty pence","The notation p means pence.","meaning")]});
D("penchant",{etymology:E("Borrowed from French penchant ‘leaning, inclination’, the present participle of pencher ‘to lean’; figuratively it is a lasting preference or tendency.",null,"pencher",null,"Etymonline, penchant (https://www.etymonline.com/word/penchant)."),contexts:[C("penchant.s1","通用","Mira has a penchant for maps and often spends her lunch break tracing old trade routes.","米拉特別喜歡地圖，常在午休時描繪古老的貿易路線。","A penchant is a lasting taste or tendency to choose a particular kind of thing.","Penchant for introduces the favored interest; and adds a habitual example.","Her repeated map-related activity shows a strong enduring preference.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","His penchant for quiet study was obvious because he avoided books and spent every evening seeking noisy parties.","His penchant for lively parties was obvious because he avoided books and spent every evening seeking noisy gatherings.","Avoiding books and repeatedly choosing noisy parties show a preference for parties, not for quiet study.")],quiz:[Q("penchant.q1","penchant.s1","meaning","A person with a penchant for puzzles ___.",["has a strong liking for puzzles","is unable to recognize puzzles","must avoid every game"],"has a strong liking for puzzles","A penchant is a particular taste or tendency.","meaning"),Q("penchant.q2","penchant.s1","context","Which habit suggests a penchant for gardening?",["She spends free time tending plants and learning about soil.","She has never visited a garden.","She dislikes all outdoor activities."],"She spends free time tending plants and learning about soil.","Repeated attention to gardening indicates a preference.","context"),Q("penchant.q3","penchant.s1","collocation","He has a ____ for collecting unusual postcards.",["penchant","penalty","pence"],"penchant","Penchant for is the standard phrase for a strong preference.","collocation"),Q("penchant.q4","penchant.s1","word-choice","Her ____ for elaborate hats was clear from the collection in her closet.",["penchant","penal","pending"],"penchant","A lasting fondness for the hats is a penchant.","word-choice")]});
D("pencil",{etymology:E("From Old French pincel and Latin penicillus ‘painter’s brush’, literally ‘little tail’; small brushes were once used for writing before graphite sticks took the name.",null,"penicillus",null,"Etymonline, pencil (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pencil)."),contexts:[C("pencil.s1","通用","Please use a pencil to mark the map because the route may change after the survey.","請用鉛筆標記地圖，因為調查後路線可能會改變。","A pencil is a writing or drawing tool with a graphite or colored core.","Use a pencil is the instruction; because gives the reason for erasability.","Pencil marks can be changed if the route is revised."),C("pencil.s2","通用","She penciled the measurements in the margin before entering them into the final table.","她先把測量值用鉛筆寫在頁邊，再輸入正式表格。","To pencil means write or draw with a pencil.","Penciled is a transitive past verb; before gives the order.","She makes temporary written notes in pencil."),C("pencil.s3","口语","We penciled the interview in for Thursday, but the editor may need to move it.","我們暫定星期四採訪，但編輯可能需要改時間。","To pencil something in is arrange it provisionally, knowing it may change.","Penciled in is a phrasal verb; but signals that the booking is tentative.","The interview is scheduled but not yet fixed.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","They penciled in the appointment as final and unchangeable, with no possibility of moving it later.","They confirmed the appointment as final and unchangeable, with no possibility of moving it later.","Pencil in means make a provisional arrangement, not a final unchangeable one.")],quiz:[Q("pencil.q1","pencil.s1","meaning","A pencil is useful for a draft because its marks can be ___.",["erased or changed","used to sign a passport permanently","heard from across a room"],"erased or changed","Pencil marks are erasable, which suits a draft.","meaning"),Q("pencil.q2","pencil.s2","context","Which sentence uses pencil as a verb meaning write?",["She penciled a note beside the diagram.","She sharpened a wooden pencil.","She bought a pencil case."],"She penciled a note beside the diagram.","Penciled describes writing with the instrument.","context"),Q("pencil.q3","pencil.s3","meaning","If a meeting is penciled in, it is ___.",["scheduled provisionally","canceled permanently","already completed"],"scheduled provisionally","The phrasal verb means make a tentative booking.","meaning"),Q("pencil.q4","pencil.s1","word-choice","Use a ____ first so you can erase the sketch if needed.",["pencil","pendant","penalty"],"pencil","A pencil is suitable for an erasable sketch.","word-choice")]});
D("pendant",{etymology:E("From Old French pendant, originally any loose hanging part, from the present participle of pendre ‘to hang’ and Latin pendere ‘hang’.",null,"pendere",null,"Etymonline, pendant (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pendant)."),contexts:[C("pendant.s1","外貌","The silver pendant hung from a fine chain and rested just above the collar of her coat.","銀色吊墜掛在細鍊上，落在她外套衣領上方。","A pendant is a piece of jewelry that hangs from a chain around the neck.","Hung from describes attachment; and coordinates its position.","The ornament is suspended from the necklace chain.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","She wore a pendant by fastening it around her wrist like a bracelet, with no chain or hanging ornament.","She wore a bracelet around her wrist and a pendant hanging from a chain around her neck.","A pendant hangs from a necklace chain; an ornament worn as a wrist band is a bracelet.")],quiz:[Q("pendant.q1","pendant.s1","meaning","A pendant is usually ___.",["an ornament hanging from a necklace chain","a ring worn on a finger","a shoe fastener"],"an ornament hanging from a necklace chain","The jewelry hangs from a chain around the neck.","meaning"),Q("pendant.q2","pendant.s1","context","Which item is a pendant?",["A small silver charm suspended from a neck chain","A watch strapped to a wrist","A pin fixed flat to a jacket"],"A small silver charm suspended from a neck chain","The charm hangs from the necklace.","context"),Q("pendant.q3","pendant.s1","word-choice","The jeweler attached the blue stone to a chain as a ____.",["pendant","pencil","peninsula"],"pendant","The stone hangs from the chain as a pendant.","word-choice"),Q("pendant.q4","pendant.s1","meaning","The history of pendant relates to the idea of ___.",["hanging down","being written in ink","paying a legal fine"],"hanging down","Its source word is related to the French verb for hanging.","meaning")]});
D("pending",{etymology:E("From Latin pendere ‘hang’, through Anglo-French and Old French; a matter pending is figuratively hanging unresolved, and the word also means imminent or ‘while awaiting’.",null,"pendere",null,"Etymonline, pending (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pending)."),contexts:[C("pending.s1","法律","The permit application remained pending until the fire inspector reviewed the revised floor plan.","許可申請一直待決，直到消防檢查員審查修訂後的平面圖。","Pending means waiting to be decided, settled, or finished.","Remained pending is the state; until marks what ends the wait.","The application has not yet received a decision."),C("pending.s2","书面","A pending storm forced the harbor master to close the outer docks before sunset.","風暴即將來臨，港務長在日落前關閉了外側碼頭。","Pending can mean about to happen soon.","Attributive adjective before storm; forced gives the consequence.","The storm is expected soon enough to require action now."),C("pending.s3","正式","Pending a final review, the agency will keep the test results confidential.","在等待最後審查期間，機關會對檢測結果保密。","As a preposition, pending means until or while waiting for an event.","Pending a final review sets the condition and duration for confidentiality.","The results remain private during the review wait.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The application was pending after the agency had issued its final decision and no further review remained.","The application was settled after the agency issued its final decision and no further review remained.","Pending means awaiting a decision or completion; a finalized matter is no longer pending.")],quiz:[Q("pending.q1","pending.s1","meaning","A pending application ___.",["is waiting for a decision","has already been approved and closed","was never submitted"],"is waiting for a decision","Pending describes something not yet decided or completed.","meaning"),Q("pending.q2","pending.s2","context","Which event is pending?",["A storm expected to arrive within hours","A storm that passed last week","A storm ruled out by the forecast"],"A storm expected to arrive within hours","Here pending means imminent.","context"),Q("pending.q3","pending.s3","grammar","In “Pending review, the files will remain sealed,” pending means ___.",["while awaiting","because of","in addition to"],"while awaiting","As a preposition it marks the waiting period.","grammar"),Q("pending.q4","pending.s1","word-choice","The court left the case ____ until the new evidence was examined.",["pending","pendulous","pendulum"],"pending","The case is still waiting for a decision.","word-choice")]});
D("pendulous",{etymology:E("From Latin pendulus ‘hanging down’, from pendere ‘hang’ + -ous; it describes something loosely suspended and able to swing.",null,"pendere","-ous","Etymonline, pendulous (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pendulous)."),contexts:[C("pendulous.s1","通用","The pendulous seed pods swayed beneath the branches whenever a gust crossed the garden.","每當一陣風掠過花園，懸垂的種莢就在枝條下搖晃。","Pendulous means hanging loosely so that something can swing freely.","Attributive adjective before seed pods; whenever gives the repeated trigger.","The pods hang from the branches and move freely in wind.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The pendulous lantern was bolted rigidly to the wall and could not hang or swing at all.","The fixed lantern was bolted rigidly to the wall and could not hang or swing.","Pendulous describes something hanging freely; a rigidly fixed lantern is not pendulous.")],quiz:[Q("pendulous.q1","pendulous.s1","meaning","Pendulous branches are ___.",["hanging loosely and able to swing","buried under the soil","fixed flat against a wall"],"hanging loosely and able to swing","The adjective describes a hanging, swinging position.","meaning"),Q("pendulous.q2","pendulous.s1","context","Which object is pendulous?",["A loose tassel swaying beneath a curtain rod","A stone block cemented into a wall","A flat tile resting on the floor"],"A loose tassel swaying beneath a curtain rod","The tassel hangs and moves freely.","context"),Q("pendulous.q3","pendulous.s1","grammar","Choose the adjective: “The ____ fruit hung below the branch.”",["pendulous","pendulum","pendulously"],"pendulous","The blank modifies fruit and requires an adjective.","grammar"),Q("pendulous.q4","pendulous.s1","word-choice","A ____ lamp swung gently from the ceiling hook.",["pendulous","penal","perceptible"],"pendulous","The lamp hangs freely and swings.","word-choice")]});
D("pendulum",{etymology:E("From Modern Latin pendulum, a noun use of Latin pendulus ‘hanging down’, from pendere ‘hang’; a suspended weight swings under gravity.",null,"pendere","-ulum","Etymonline, pendulum (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pendulum)."),contexts:[C("pendulum.s1","物理","The pendulum swung through a smaller arc as friction gradually removed energy from the clock.","摩擦逐漸消耗時鐘的能量後，鐘擺擺動的弧度變小。","A pendulum is a weight suspended from a fixed point so it swings under gravity.","Swung is the action; as gives the gradual change.","The suspended weight moves back and forth around its fixed point."),C("pendulum.s2","比喻","After years of strict rules, public opinion’s pendulum swung toward greater personal freedom.","多年嚴格規範後，輿論風向轉向更大的個人自由。","Figuratively, a pendulum is a situation that shifts from one extreme to another.","Pendulum is a metaphorical subject; toward names the new position.","Opinion reverses direction from a prior extreme, like a swinging weight.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The pendulum stayed permanently at one extreme and never shifted toward another position.","The pendulum swung away from one extreme toward another position.","The figurative pendulum sense implies change or movement between positions, not permanent immobility.")],quiz:[Q("pendulum.q1","pendulum.s1","meaning","A clock pendulum is a weight that ___.",["swings from a fixed point","rolls along the floor","measures ink in a pen"],"swings from a fixed point","The physical object is suspended and swings under gravity.","meaning"),Q("pendulum.q2","pendulum.s2","context","If a political pendulum swings, public views ___.",["shift from one position or extreme toward another","remain identical forever","disappear from discussion"],"shift from one position or extreme toward another","The metaphor describes change in direction or preference.","context"),Q("pendulum.q3","pendulum.s1","word-choice","The clock’s brass ____ kept time by swinging steadily.",["pendulum","pendant","peninsula"],"pendulum","The suspended weight in a clock is its pendulum.","word-choice"),Q("pendulum.q4","pendulum.s2","meaning","A pendulum shift in fashion suggests that trends ___.",["swing back and forth between styles","never change","are measured only by clocks"],"swing back and forth between styles","The metaphor compares changing trends to a swinging weight.","meaning")]});
D("penetrate",{etymology:E("From Latin penetrare ‘put or get into, enter’; it first meant pierce through a barrier and developed figurative senses of understanding deeply or gaining entry to a market or group.",null,"penetrare",null,"Etymonline, penetrate (https://www.etymonline.com/word/penetrate)."),contexts:[C("penetrate.s1","通用","The insulated glass prevented the cold wind from penetrating the cabin during the night.","隔熱玻璃阻止冷風吹進小屋，度過了整個夜晚。","Penetrate means go into or through something, especially a barrier.","Prevented the wind from penetrating uses the gerund after from.","The glass stops the wind from entering the cabin."),C("penetrate.s2","书面","Only after reading the full report did the analyst penetrate the logic behind the unusual pricing scheme.","分析師讀完整份報告後，才看透這套特殊定價方案背後的邏輯。","Penetrate can mean succeed in understanding something difficult or hidden.","Did the analyst penetrate is emphatic inversion after Only; behind introduces hidden logic.","The report allows the analyst to grasp the reasoning beneath the surface."),C("penetrate.s3","商业","The small manufacturer hopes to penetrate the European market with a repairable, low-cost pump.","這家小型製造商希望以可維修、低成本的水泵打入歐洲市場。","Penetrate can mean become accepted into a market, group, or area.","Hopes to penetrate is followed by the target market; with gives the product strategy.","The company aims to establish a presence among European buyers.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The cold air penetrated the sealed cabin because it remained entirely outside and never entered through any opening.","The cold air failed to penetrate the sealed cabin because it remained outside and never entered through any opening.","Penetrate means enter or pass through; air that remains outside has not penetrated the cabin.")],quiz:[Q("penetrate.q1","penetrate.s1","meaning","A beam of light penetrates a curtain when it ___.",["passes through it","stops before reaching it","changes into sound"],"passes through it","The physical sense is enter or pass through a barrier.","meaning"),Q("penetrate.q2","penetrate.s2","context","Which analyst penetrates a difficult argument?",["One who understands its hidden reasoning","One who refuses to read it","One who copies the title only"],"One who understands its hidden reasoning","This figurative sense is to understand deeply.","context"),Q("penetrate.q3","penetrate.s3","meaning","A company trying to penetrate a new market hopes to ___.",["gain access and establish itself there","leave the market immediately","hide its products from buyers"],"gain access and establish itself there","The business sense means enter and find acceptance in a market.","meaning"),Q("penetrate.q4","penetrate.s1","verb-form","Choose the past form: “The sunlight ____ the dense canopy.”",["penetrated","penetrate","penetrating"],"penetrated","The regular past form adds -d after final e.","verb-form")]});
D("penetrating",{etymology:E("The adjective is the present participle of penetrate; it describes either sharp physical force or unusually quick, deep understanding.",null,"penetrate","-ing","Etymonline, penetrating (https://www.etymonline.com/word/penetrating)."),contexts:[C("penetrating.s1","通用","Her penetrating question exposed an assumption that the committee had never tested.","她敏銳的提問揭露了委員會從未檢驗過的一項假設。","Penetrating means quick and deep in understanding, reaching the heart of a matter.","Attributive adjective before question; that introduces the assumption exposed.","The question gets to a hidden premise rather than staying on the surface."),C("penetrating.s2","通用","A penetrating wind cut through the hikers’ coats as they crossed the exposed ridge.","健行者越過開闊山脊時，刺骨的風穿透了外套。","Penetrating can describe a force so sharp or strong that it goes through a barrier.","Attributive adjective before wind; as introduces the setting.","The wind is strong enough to be felt through the coats.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The penetrating cold stayed entirely outside the sealed coat and could not be felt by the hiker.","The mild cold stayed outside the sealed coat and could not be felt by the hiker.","Penetrating cold is sharply felt through clothing; cold that cannot be felt does not penetrate.")],quiz:[Q("penetrating.q1","penetrating.s1","meaning","A penetrating observation is ___.",["deep and perceptive","unrelated to the issue","too faint to understand"],"deep and perceptive","The adjective can describe insight reaching a matter’s core.","meaning"),Q("penetrating.q2","penetrating.s2","context","Which weather is penetrating?",["A sharp wind felt through several layers of clothing","A warm breeze blocked by a closed window","A calm sunny afternoon"],"A sharp wind felt through several layers of clothing","The force is strong enough to pass through a barrier.","context"),Q("penetrating.q3","penetrating.s1","grammar","Choose the adjective: “The interviewer asked a ____ question.”",["penetrating","penetration","penetrate"],"penetrating","The blank modifies question and requires an adjective.","grammar"),Q("penetrating.q4","penetrating.s1","word-choice","The detective’s ____ insight revealed the motive behind the disguise.",["penetrating","penal","pence"],"penetrating","The insight is sharp and gets to the hidden explanation.","word-choice")]});
D("penetration",{etymology:E("From Latin penetrationem, a noun of action from penetrare ‘put or get into’; the word names entry through material and, figuratively, deep insight.",null,"penetrare","-ation","Etymonline, penetration (https://www.etymonline.com/word/penetration)."),contexts:[C("penetration.s1","通用","The coating improves water penetration into the dry soil without letting the surface wash away.","這層覆蓋物能改善水分滲入乾燥土壤，同時避免表土被沖走。","Penetration is the action of going into or through a material, area, or market.","Improves water penetration identifies the process; without states a prevented result.","Water enters the soil rather than remaining on its surface."),C("penetration.s2","通用","Her penetration of the witness’s evasive answer helped the team see what had been left unsaid.","她看穿證人的閃爍其詞，讓團隊明白哪些事沒有說出口。","Penetration can mean the ability to understand something difficult or hidden.","Penetration of the answer is the subject; helped introduces the result.","She recognizes the hidden meaning behind the evasive words.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The soil’s water penetration was zero because every drop soaked beneath the surface immediately.","The soil’s water penetration was rapid because every drop soaked beneath the surface immediately.","Water soaking into soil is penetration; zero penetration would mean it stayed on top.")],quiz:[Q("penetration.q1","penetration.s1","meaning","Water penetration into soil means water ___.",["enters the soil","stays entirely above the ground","turns into sunlight"],"enters the soil","The physical noun names movement into a material.","meaning"),Q("penetration.q2","penetration.s2","context","A lawyer’s penetration of a complicated argument is her ability to ___.",["understand its hidden logic","make it harder to read","copy its punctuation"],"understand its hidden logic","This sense is insight into something difficult.","context"),Q("penetration.q3","penetration.s1","word-formation","The noun naming the action of penetrating is ___.",["penetration","penetrative","penetrate"],"penetration","The suffix -ation forms the noun for the action or process.","word-formation"),Q("penetration.q4","penetration.s2","word-choice","Her analytical ____ revealed the unstated assumption.",["penetration","penalty","peninsula"],"penetration","The sentence describes the ability to see into a difficult argument.","word-choice")]});
D("penguin",{etymology:E("The bird name was first recorded for the great auk and shifted to the Antarctic swimming bird by the late sixteenth century; its ultimate origin is unknown, and the Welsh pen gwyn explanation is unproven.",null,null,null,"Etymonline, penguin (https://www.etymonline.com/word/penguin)."),contexts:[C("penguin.s1","动物","A penguin balanced on the ice, then slid into the water to catch small fish.","一隻企鵝在冰上站穩後，滑進水裡捕捉小魚。","A penguin is a black-and-white seabird with flipper-like wings that cannot fly but swims well.","Balanced and slid are coordinated actions; then gives their order.","The bird’s wings function as flippers in the water.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The penguin flew over the ice on broad wings before diving into the sea to catch fish.","The penguin waddled over the ice before diving into the sea to catch fish.","Penguins cannot fly; they move on land by walking or waddling and swim in water.")],quiz:[Q("penguin.q1","penguin.s1","meaning","Penguins are seabirds that ___.",["swim well but cannot fly","fly long distances with feathered wings","live only in dry deserts"],"swim well but cannot fly","Their short wings act as flippers and support swimming.","meaning"),Q("penguin.q2","penguin.s1","context","Which observation fits a penguin?",["It dives into cold water to catch fish.","It soars above a forest to hunt mice.","It builds a nest in a hot desert dune."],"It dives into cold water to catch fish.","Penguins are swimming seabirds that feed in the water.","context"),Q("penguin.q3","penguin.s1","word-choice","The black-and-white bird waddled across the ice: a ____.",["penguin","pendulum","peninsula"],"penguin","A penguin is the flightless seabird on the ice.","word-choice"),Q("penguin.q4","penguin.s1","meaning","Why are a penguin’s wings useful underwater?",["They act like flippers for swimming.","They lift the bird into long-distance flight.","They store food for winter."],"They act like flippers for swimming.","Penguin wings are adapted for movement through water.","meaning")]});
D("penicillin",{etymology:E("Named from Penicillium notatum, the mold from which it was first obtained; the scientific genus name comes from Latin penicillus ‘small brush’, describing the mold’s brushlike cell structures.",null,"Penicillium / penicillus",null,"Etymonline, penicillin (https://www.etymonline.com/word/penicillin)."),contexts:[C("penicillin.s1","通用","The doctor prescribed penicillin for the bacterial infection and told the patient to finish the full course.","醫師為細菌感染開了青黴素，並提醒病人完成整個療程。","Penicillin is a drug from mold that kills or stops the growth of many bacteria.","Prescribed penicillin for identifies its use; and adds the instruction.","The medicine treats susceptible bacterial infection, so the full course matters.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The doctor prescribed penicillin for a viral cold because the drug kills viruses but has no effect on bacteria.","The doctor prescribed a suitable antiviral medicine for the viral illness because penicillin acts against bacteria, not viruses.","Penicillin is an antibacterial drug; it does not kill viruses such as those causing a common cold.")],quiz:[Q("penicillin.q1","penicillin.s1","meaning","Penicillin is an antibiotic that acts against many ___.",["bacteria","rocks","viruses only"],"bacteria","Penicillin kills or inhibits many bacteria.","meaning"),Q("penicillin.q2","penicillin.s1","context","For which condition might a doctor prescribe penicillin?",["A susceptible bacterial infection","A broken bone with no infection","A viral cold that needs no antibacterial treatment"],"A susceptible bacterial infection","Penicillin can treat infections caused by susceptible bacteria.","context"),Q("penicillin.q3","penicillin.s1","word-choice","The clinician prescribed ____ to treat the bacterial infection.",["penicillin","penmanship","peninsula"],"penicillin","Penicillin is the antibacterial medicine.","word-choice"),Q("penicillin.q4","penicillin.s1","meaning","Why should a patient not assume penicillin cures every illness?",["It acts on many bacteria, not on every cause of illness.","It is a writing instrument.","It only treats broken bones."],"It acts on many bacteria, not on every cause of illness.","Antibiotics do not treat every kind of infection or condition.","meaning")]});
D("peninsula",{etymology:E("From Latin paeninsula, literally ‘almost an island’, formed from paene ‘almost’ + insula ‘island’.","paene","insula",null,"Etymonline, peninsula (https://www.etymonline.com/word/peninsula)."),contexts:[C("peninsula.s1","地理","The coastal highway curves around the peninsula, with water on both sides for most of the drive.","沿海道路環繞半島蜿蜒而行，大部分路段兩側都是海水。","A peninsula is land surrounded by water on three sides and joined to a larger landmass.","Around the peninsula names the route; with introduces its physical setting.","The land remains connected to the mainland despite water on three sides.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The island was a peninsula because it was completely surrounded by water and had no connection to a larger landmass.","The land was an island because it was completely surrounded by water and had no connection to a larger landmass.","A peninsula remains attached to a larger landmass; completely isolated land is an island.")],quiz:[Q("peninsula.q1","peninsula.s1","meaning","A peninsula is land that ___.",["projects into water while remaining joined to a larger landmass","is surrounded by water with no land connection","lies entirely under the sea"],"projects into water while remaining joined to a larger landmass","The land has water on several sides but stays attached to the mainland.","meaning"),Q("peninsula.q2","peninsula.s1","context","Which landform is a peninsula?",["A region with sea on three sides and a narrow land neck","A small island separated by deep water","A mountain entirely surrounded by desert"],"A region with sea on three sides and a narrow land neck","It remains attached by a narrow strip of land.","context"),Q("peninsula.q3","peninsula.s1","word-choice","The city occupies a narrow ____ extending into the bay.",["peninsula","pendant","penalty"],"peninsula","A narrow landform extending into water while attached is a peninsula.","word-choice"),Q("peninsula.q4","peninsula.s1","word-formation","The Latin source of peninsula literally means ___.",["almost an island","small writing brush","legal punishment"],"almost an island","The Latin compound combines paene ‘almost’ and insula ‘island’.","word-formation")]});
D("penmanship",{etymology:E("Formed from penman + -ship; penman combined pen + man for a skilled writer, and -ship denotes a quality or skill, yielding ‘handwriting’.",null,"pen + man","-ship","Etymonline, penmanship (https://www.etymonline.com/word/penmanship)."),contexts:[C("penmanship.s1","教育","The teacher praised Omar’s penmanship because every letter was clear and evenly spaced.","老師稱讚奧馬爾的字跡，因為每個字母都清楚且間距均勻。","Penmanship is the style or quality of someone’s handwriting.","Praised penmanship is the object; because gives the reason.","The letters’ clarity and spacing show skilled handwriting.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The teacher criticized the student’s penmanship because the handwritten page was perfectly legible and carefully spaced.","The teacher praised the student’s penmanship because the handwritten page was perfectly legible and carefully spaced.","Legible, carefully spaced writing is good penmanship, not poor handwriting.")],quiz:[Q("penmanship.q1","penmanship.s1","meaning","Penmanship refers to the quality of someone’s ___.",["handwriting","speaking voice","running speed"],"handwriting","The noun concerns how someone writes by hand.","meaning"),Q("penmanship.q2","penmanship.s1","context","Which page shows good penmanship?",["The letters are neat, readable, and evenly spaced.","The page is blank.","The words are smudged beyond recognition."],"The letters are neat, readable, and evenly spaced.","Legible, consistent handwriting is good penmanship.","context"),Q("penmanship.q3","penmanship.s1","word-choice","The calligraphy teacher helped improve her students’ ____.",["penmanship","peninsula","penicillin"],"penmanship","The teacher works on their handwriting skill.","word-choice"),Q("penmanship.q4","penmanship.s1","meaning","A note with clear letter shapes and spacing has neat ___.",["penmanship","penury","penalty"],"penmanship","Penmanship is the style or quality of handwriting.","meaning")]});
D("penny",{etymology:E("From Old English penig/penning and Proto-Germanic *panninga-, a coin name of unknown ultimate origin; no deeper root is asserted.",null,null,null,"Etymonline, penny (https://www.etymonline.com/word/penny)."),contexts:[C("penny.s1","金融","The machine accepted a one-pound coin but rejected a single penny that had been bent in half.","機器收下一枚一英鎊硬幣，卻拒收一枚被折彎的便士。","A British penny is a coin worth one hundredth of a pound.","Accepted and rejected contrast two coins; that clause explains the rejection.","The bent coin may not be recognized by the machine."),C("penny.s2","口语","I would not spend a penny on that broken charger; it stopped working after one use.","那個壞掉的充電器我一分錢也不會花；它用過一次就壞了。","In informal American usage, penny can mean a cent or a very small amount of money.","Would not spend a penny is an idiom emphasizing refusal to pay.","The speaker considers the charger not worth even a small sum.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The cashier returned one penny, a coin worth one hundred pounds, as change.","The cashier returned one pound, a unit worth one hundred pence, as change.","A penny is a small denomination; it is not worth one hundred pounds.")],quiz:[Q("penny.q1","penny.s1","meaning","In Britain, a penny is worth ___.",["one hundredth of a pound","one whole pound","one hundred pounds"],"one hundredth of a pound","The British pound is divided into 100 pence.","meaning"),Q("penny.q2","penny.s2","context","In “I wouldn’t pay a penny for it,” penny means ___.",["a very small amount of money","a full house","a legal sentence"],"a very small amount of money","The informal phrase emphasizes that the item is worth almost nothing.","context"),Q("penny.q3","penny.s1","plural","Choose the British currency plural: “Three ____ were left in the tray.”",["pence","pennys","pennieses"],"pence","Pence is the standard plural unit in British currency.","plural"),Q("penny.q4","penny.s2","word-choice","The damaged toy is not worth a ____ to me.",["penny","peninsula","pendulum"],"penny","The phrase means it is worth no small amount of money.","word-choice")]});
