D("pennycress",{etymology:E("A compound of penny and cress; the plant name refers to the round, flat seed pods that resemble small coins.",null,"penny + cress",null,"Etymonline, pennycress (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pennycress)."),contexts:[C("pennycress.s1","植物","The botanist identified pennycress by its small, round seed discs growing above the roadside leaves.","植物學家根據路邊葉片上方長出的圓形小種子盤，辨認出菥蓂。","Pennycress is an annual herb whose seed discs resemble small coins.","By introduces the identifying feature; growing above modifies seed discs.","The coin-like seed pods are a characteristic feature of the plant.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","Pennycress is a large ocean fish whose scales are shaped like coins.","Pennycress is a small flowering herb whose seed pods are shaped like coins.","Pennycress is a plant, not a fish; the name refers to its coin-shaped seed pods.")],quiz:[Q("pennycress.q1","pennycress.s1","meaning","What part of pennycress resembles a penny?",["Its flat, round seed pod","Its flower’s scent","Its underground stem"],"Its flat, round seed pod","The common name points to the coin-like seed discs.","meaning"),Q("pennycress.q2","pennycress.s1","context","Where is a botanist most likely to find pennycress growing?",["In a field or along a roadside","On a coral reef","Inside a mammal’s stomach"],"In a field or along a roadside","Pennycress is an annual herb that grows on land.","context"),Q("pennycress.q3","pennycress.s1","word-choice","The annual herb with coin-shaped seed discs is called ____.",["pennycress","penury","pension"],"pennycress","Pennycress names the herb whose seed pods look like small coins.","word-choice"),Q("pennycress.q4","pennycress.s1","word-formation","Why does the name pennycress include penny?",["The seed discs are round and coin-like.","The plant was used to print money.","It grows only beside banks."],"The seed discs are round and coin-like.","The visual resemblance to a small coin motivates the first part of the plant name.","word-formation")]});
D("pension",{etymology:E("From French pension and Latin pensio ‘payment’, from pendere ‘weigh, pay’; the word first referred to a payment and also developed a verb sense of retiring someone on such pay.",null,"pendere","-sion","Etymonline, pension (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pension)."),contexts:[C("pension.s1","金融","After thirty years at the factory, Mei receives a monthly pension that covers part of her rent.","梅在工廠工作三十年後，每月領取一筆養老金，用來支付部分房租。","A pension is a regular payment to a retired person or someone unable to work.","Receives a monthly pension identifies the recurring payment; that clause gives its use.","The money continues after the employee’s working years."),C("pension.s2","劳动","The airline chose to pension the pilot at sixty-five and continue his retirement payments.","航空公司決定讓這名飛行員在六十五歲退休，並繼續支付他的退休金。","To pension someone is to retire them while providing a pension.","Pension is a verb with the pilot as its object; at sixty-five marks the age.","The employer ends his active service and pays retirement income.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The company pensioned its new intern to begin her first week of work and stop all retirement payments.","The company hired its new intern to begin her first week of work; pensioned would mean retiring her with pension payments.","Pension as a verb means retire someone on a pension, not bring a new employee into work.")],quiz:[Q("pension.q1","pension.s1","meaning","What is a pension in the financial sense?",["A regular payment to a retired person","A one-time fee to enter a museum","A loan for buying a bicycle"],"A regular payment to a retired person","A pension provides continuing income after retirement or inability to work.","meaning"),Q("pension.q2","pension.s2","context","If an employer pensions a worker, what happens?",["The worker retires and receives pension payments.","The worker is promoted to a new position.","The worker is asked to repay a salary."],"The worker retires and receives pension payments.","The verb means to retire someone while paying a pension.","context"),Q("pension.q3","pension.s1","word-choice","She saves part of her salary because she hopes to live on a ____ after retirement.",["pension","pepper","pentagon"],"pension","A pension is retirement income paid regularly.","word-choice"),Q("pension.q4","pension.s2","grammar","Choose the verb in “The firm pensioned two senior pilots last year.”",["pensioned","pension","pensioner"],"pensioned","Pensioned is the past-tense verb describing the firm’s action.","grammar")]});
D("pensive",{etymology:E("From Old French pensif, from penser ‘think’, ultimately from Latin pensare ‘weigh, consider’; the adjective describes serious, often somewhat sad thought.",null,"pensare",null,"Etymonline, pensive (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pensive)."),contexts:[C("pensive.s1","通用","Alone by the station window, Jun gave a pensive look as he reread the letter from home.","俊獨自坐在車站窗邊，重讀家裡寄來的信時神情沉思而略帶憂鬱。","Pensive means quietly and seriously thoughtful, sometimes sad.","Pensive modifies look; as introduces the moment when the expression appears.","The letter prompts quiet reflection rather than a cheerful or distracted mood.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","After hearing the sad news, he looked pensive, laughing loudly and thinking of nothing at all.","After hearing the sad news, he looked pensive, sitting quietly and thinking about what had happened.","A pensive person is quietly thoughtful; loud laughter and no reflection contradict that description.")],quiz:[Q("pensive.q1","pensive.s1","meaning","Someone who is pensive is usually ___.",["quietly thoughtful, perhaps a little sad","carefree and unable to focus","angry and eager to argue"],"quietly thoughtful, perhaps a little sad","Pensive describes serious reflection, sometimes with sadness.","meaning"),Q("pensive.q2","pensive.s1","context","Which scene best fits a pensive mood?",["A traveler silently reflects on a difficult goodbye.","A child shouts excitedly during a game.","A chef quickly reads a recipe without pausing."],"A traveler silently reflects on a difficult goodbye.","Quiet reflection after a goodbye is pensive.","context"),Q("pensive.q3","pensive.s1","word-choice","She grew ____ while considering whether to leave her hometown.",["pensive","peppery","pendulous"],"pensive","The decision leads her into serious, quiet thought.","word-choice"),Q("pensive.q4","pensive.s1","meaning","Which detail supports calling a face pensive?",["The person pauses, looking down while thinking deeply.","The person grins while telling a joke.","The person runs without noticing anything."],"The person pauses, looking down while thinking deeply.","A pensive expression suggests thoughtful concentration, sometimes sadness.","meaning")]});
D("pent-up",{etymology:E("Pent is an older past form of pen ‘confine’; pent-up combines it with up to describe feelings or energy kept shut in without release.",null,"pen","up","Etymonline, pent-up (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pent-up)."),contexts:[C("pent-up.s1","心理","After months of delays, the team released its pent-up frustration during an unusually candid meeting.","延誤數月後，團隊在一次格外坦率的會議中宣洩了累積已久的挫折感。","Pent-up describes feelings or energy that have been confined and not expressed.","Pent-up modifies frustration; after introduces the cause and during marks when it emerged.","The emotion had built up without an earlier outlet.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The runner felt pent-up after a long race because all her energy had been released and nothing remained inside.","The runner felt exhausted after a long race; pent-up would describe energy held in without release.","Pent-up means restrained or accumulated, not already spent or released.")],quiz:[Q("pent-up.q1","pent-up.s1","meaning","Pent-up anger is anger that has been ___.",["held back and not expressed","forgotten immediately","shown openly from the start"],"held back and not expressed","Pent-up feelings are confined without an outlet.","meaning"),Q("pent-up.q2","pent-up.s1","context","Which action might release pent-up energy?",["Taking a brisk run after sitting indoors all day","Keeping still and refusing every activity","Falling asleep before feeling restless"],"Taking a brisk run after sitting indoors all day","The run provides an outlet for energy that had been held in.","context"),Q("pent-up.q3","pent-up.s1","word-choice","The children’s ____ excitement burst out when the doors finally opened.",["pent-up","perceptible","pensive"],"pent-up","The excitement had been held back while they waited.","word-choice"),Q("pent-up.q4","pent-up.s1","word-formation","The element pent in pent-up is connected with the idea of ___.",["being confined","being counted five times","being paid regularly"],"being confined","Pent is an older form related to pen, ‘confine’, which motivates this adjective.","word-formation")]});
D("pentagon",{etymology:E("From Greek pentagōnon, neuter of pentagōnos ‘five-angled’, from pente ‘five’ and gōnia ‘angle’; it names a five-sided plane figure.",null,"pente + gōnia",null,"Etymonline, pentagon (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pentagon)."),contexts:[C("pentagon.s1","数学","The designer drew a regular pentagon and marked each of its five sides with the same length.","設計者畫出一個正五邊形，並把五條邊標成相同長度。","A pentagon is a plane figure with five sides and five angles.","Regular modifies the figure; each of its five sides states the defining count.","The equal sides distinguish this regular pentagon, while the five-side count defines the shape.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","A pentagon has four sides, so the classroom window is a pentagon.","A quadrilateral has four sides; a pentagon has five, so the classroom window is not a pentagon.","The prefix penta- means five; a four-sided figure cannot be a pentagon.")],quiz:[Q("pentagon.q1","pentagon.s1","meaning","How many sides does a pentagon have?",["Five","Four","Seven"],"Five","Pentagon names a plane figure with five sides and five angles.","meaning"),Q("pentagon.q2","pentagon.s1","context","Which shape is a pentagon?",["A closed figure with five straight sides","A closed figure with three sides","A circle with no corners"],"A closed figure with five straight sides","Five sides define the pentagon among these choices.","context"),Q("pentagon.q3","pentagon.s1","word-choice","The school emblem is a five-sided figure, a ____.",["pentagon","pendulum","perigee"],"pentagon","The geometric name for a five-sided plane figure is pentagon.","word-choice"),Q("pentagon.q4","pentagon.s1","word-formation","In pentagon, the Greek element pente means ___.",["five","angle","circle"],"five","Pente is the Greek numeral ‘five’ in the word.","word-formation")]});
D("penury",{etymology:E("From Latin penuria ‘scarcity, want’, of uncertain deeper origin; the English noun refers to extreme poverty or lack of necessities.",null,"penuria",null,"Etymonline, penury (https://www.etymonline.com/word/penury)."),contexts:[C("penury.s1","社会","The report described families living in penury, without reliable heat, medicine, or enough food.","報告描述了生活極度貧困的家庭，他們缺乏穩定供暖、藥品和足夠食物。","Penury is the state of being extremely poor.","Living in penury characterizes the families; without lists necessities they lack.","The shortages show severe poverty, not merely a modest budget.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The retired executive lived in penury, owning three villas and spending freely on luxury travel.","The retired executive lived in comfort, owning three villas and spending freely on luxury travel.","Penury means extreme poverty, which conflicts with abundant wealth and luxury spending.")],quiz:[Q("penury.q1","penury.s1","meaning","A household in penury is ___.",["extremely poor","wealthy beyond need","temporarily busy"],"extremely poor","Penury is severe poverty or want.","meaning"),Q("penury.q2","penury.s1","context","Which evidence best suggests penury?",["A family cannot afford enough food or basic heating.","A family compares two expensive holiday homes.","A family saves for a new sports car."],"A family cannot afford enough food or basic heating.","Lack of basic necessities signals extreme poverty.","context"),Q("penury.q3","penury.s1","word-choice","The charity opened a shelter for people driven into ____ by the economic crisis.",["penury","pentagon","peppermint"],"penury","The sentence describes people pushed into severe poverty.","word-choice"),Q("penury.q4","penury.s1","meaning","Which is closest in meaning to penury?",["destitution","abundance","leisure"],"destitution","Destitution is extreme poverty and lack of necessities.","meaning")]});
D("people",{etymology:E("From Anglo-French poeple and Old French pueple, from Latin populus ‘people’; the English word has human, civic, ethnic, and verb uses.",null,"populus",null,"Etymonline, people (https://www.etymonline.com/word/people)."),contexts:[C("people.s1","通用","People gathered quietly outside the library to hear the author read from her new book.","人們安靜地聚集在圖書館外，聆聽作者朗讀新書。","People means human beings considered collectively.","People is the plural subject of gathered; to hear gives their purpose.","The sentence refers to a group of individuals, not a government or ethnic nation."),C("people.s2","政治","The constitution says the people may choose their representatives in a free election.","憲法規定，人民可以在自由選舉中選出自己的代表。","The people can mean a country’s ordinary citizens, especially in relation to government.","The people is the subject of may choose; their representatives signals the civic sense.","Here people means citizens who hold political rights."),C("people.s4","文学","For generations, fishing families have peopled the island’s eastern villages.","數代以來，漁民家庭一直居住在島嶼東部的村落。","To people a place means live in it or fill it with inhabitants.","Peopled is a transitive verb with villages as object; for generations gives duration.","The villages have residents; people here is a verb, not the plural noun.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The constitution gave the people no citizens at all, because people means only the elected government ministers.","The constitution gave ordinary citizens a voice, because the people can mean the country’s citizens as a body.","People can mean ordinary citizens collectively; it does not mean only government ministers.")],quiz:[Q("people.q1","people.s1","meaning","In “People filled the hall,” people means ___.",["human beings as a group","a single elected official","a written law"],"human beings as a group","This is the ordinary plural-noun sense of people.","meaning"),Q("people.q2","people.s2","context","In a democracy, “the people elected a council” refers to ___.",["the country’s citizens","the council building","foreign tourists only"],"the country’s citizens","The civic sense identifies ordinary citizens who choose representatives.","context"),Q("people.q3","people.s4","grammar","In “Settlers peopled the valley,” peopled is a ___.",["verb meaning inhabited or filled with residents","plural noun meaning several persons","adjective meaning popular"],"verb meaning inhabited or filled with residents","Peopled takes the valley as its object and means to inhabit it.","grammar"),Q("people.q4","people.s3","meaning","A people with a shared culture is ___.",["a community or nation with its own culture","any two strangers in a queue","a government office"],"a community or nation with its own culture","This sense uses people for an ethnic or cultural community.","meaning")]});
D("pepper",{etymology:E("From Old English pipor and Latin piper, ultimately from Greek peperi and an Asian source; the spice name was extended to unrelated capsicum fruits, and the verb means season or pelt with many things.",null,"piper",null,"Etymonline, pepper (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pepper)."),contexts:[C("pepper.s1","飲食","A pinch of black pepper sharpened the soup without making it taste as hot as chili.","一撮黑胡椒讓湯的味道更鮮明，卻沒有辣椒那麼辣。","Pepper is a pungent spice made from dried berries.","A pinch of black pepper is the subject; without contrasts its taste with chili.","The seasoning is the ground spice, distinct from the vegetable called pepper."),C("pepper.s2","飲食","She sliced a red pepper into strips and added the crisp pieces to the salad.","她把紅甜椒切成條，加入沙拉中。","A pepper can be a hollow fruit eaten as a vegetable; some kinds are hot.","A red pepper is the object of sliced; the salad context signals the vegetable.","The fruit is a capsicum vegetable, not ground peppercorn spice."),C("pepper.s3","通用","The hail peppered the greenhouse roof with small dents during the sudden storm.","突來的暴風雨中，冰雹在溫室屋頂打出許多小凹痕。","To pepper something is to hit or cover it repeatedly with many small things.","Peppered is a transitive verb with the roof as object; with small dents states the result.","Many hailstones strike across the roof, giving the figurative sense of repeated small impacts.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","He sliced black pepper into the salad as a crunchy vegetable and ground a red bell-pepper fruit over the soup.","He sliced a red bell pepper into the salad as a crunchy vegetable and ground black pepper over the soup.","A bell pepper is the vegetable; black pepper is the dried-berry spice that is ground.")],quiz:[Q("pepper.q1","pepper.s1","meaning","Black pepper used at the table is ___.",["a spice made from dried berries","a leafy herb eaten as lettuce","a sweet fruit juice"],"a spice made from dried berries","The spice is made from dried peppercorn berries.","meaning"),Q("pepper.q2","pepper.s2","context","Which item is a vegetable pepper?",["A hollow red fruit stuffed and baked","A jar of ground black seasoning","A whole dried berry in a spice mill"],"A hollow red fruit stuffed and baked","The capsicum fruit is eaten as a vegetable.","context"),Q("pepper.q3","pepper.s3","meaning","If hail peppers a roof, the hail ___.",["strikes it repeatedly with many small pieces","covers it in a single smooth sheet","quietly melts beneath it"],"strikes it repeatedly with many small pieces","The verb means to hit or cover with numerous small items.","meaning"),Q("pepper.q4","pepper.s2","word-choice","The recipe asks for one green ____ to be diced with the onions.",["pepper","penury","pension"],"pepper","A green pepper is the hollow vegetable fruit used in the recipe.","word-choice")]});
D("peppermint",{etymology:E("A compound of pepper and mint, recorded for the pungent mint plant; it also names the strongly flavored sweet made with its oil.",null,"pepper + mint",null,"Etymonline, peppermint (https://www.etymonline.com/word/peppermint)."),contexts:[C("peppermint.s1","飲食","After dinner, Ruth chose a peppermint to freshen her mouth and tucked the wrapper into her bag.","晚餐後，露絲拿了一顆薄荷糖清新口氣，並把包裝紙收進包裡。","Peppermint can name the fresh-tasting plant or a sweet flavored with it.","A peppermint is the object of chose; the wrapper indicates the candy sense.","The sweet is flavored with the cool, strong taste of peppermint oil.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","He chewed a peppermint to make his mouth taste strongly of roasted coffee beans.","He chewed a peppermint to give his mouth a cool, minty taste.","Peppermint has a characteristic fresh mint flavor, not a roasted-coffee flavor.")],quiz:[Q("peppermint.q1","peppermint.s1","meaning","Peppermint is associated with a strong, fresh taste from a ___.",["mint plant","grain of rice","citrus tree bark"],"mint plant","Peppermint names a mint plant and its characteristic flavor.","meaning"),Q("peppermint.q2","peppermint.s1","context","What might someone unwrap after a meal to freshen their breath?",["A peppermint sweet","A raw potato","A lump of clay"],"A peppermint sweet","Peppermint sweets carry the plant’s fresh flavor.","context"),Q("peppermint.q3","peppermint.s1","word-choice","The tea has a cool herbal flavor because it contains ____ leaves.",["peppermint","penury","pentagon"],"peppermint","Peppermint leaves give tea a strong, fresh mint taste.","word-choice"),Q("peppermint.q4","peppermint.s1","meaning","Which product is flavored with peppermint?",["A mint sweet","A plain glass jar","A metal spoon"],"A mint sweet","Peppermint flavor commonly appears in sweets and other foods.","meaning")]});
D("peppery",{etymology:E("Formed from pepper + -y; the adjective first describes a hot, sharp flavor and also a person or manner that is irritable and sharp in speech.",null,"pepper","-y","Etymonline, peppery (https://www.etymonline.com/word/peppery)."),contexts:[C("peppery.s1","飲食","The stew had a peppery finish that warmed the tongue but did not overwhelm the herbs.","燉菜帶有胡椒般的辛辣尾韻，讓舌頭暖起來，卻沒有蓋過香草味。","Peppery means hot and sharp in flavor, like pepper.","Peppery modifies finish; that clause describes how it affects the tongue.","The word describes the dish’s pungent taste, not a person’s temper."),C("peppery.s2","通用","The usually patient editor grew peppery when the same careless typo appeared for the fourth time.","一向有耐心的編輯看到同一個粗心錯字第四次出現時，變得易怒起來。","Peppery can mean quick to anger and sharp in speech.","Peppery modifies editor; when gives the trigger for the change in mood.","The repeated error makes the editor irritable rather than giving the editor a spicy taste.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The peppery editor remained perfectly calm, spoke gently, and showed no irritation at repeated errors.","The peppery editor grew irritable and spoke sharply after repeated errors.","The temper sense of peppery means irritable and sharp, which conflicts with perfect calm and gentleness.")],quiz:[Q("peppery.q1","peppery.s1","meaning","A peppery sauce tastes ___.",["hot and sharp","sweet and bland","cold and metallic"],"hot and sharp","Peppery describes a pungent, spicy flavor.","meaning"),Q("peppery.q2","peppery.s2","context","A peppery reply is most likely ___.",["irritable and sharply worded","quietly affectionate","carefully neutral"],"irritable and sharply worded","The figurative sense describes a sharp temper or manner.","context"),Q("peppery.q3","peppery.s1","word-choice","The chef added extra chili for a ____ kick in the soup.",["peppery","pensive","perceptive"],"peppery","The sentence describes a hot, sharp taste.","word-choice"),Q("peppery.q4","peppery.s2","meaning","Why was the response called peppery?",["It sounded impatient and cutting.","It contained ground spice.","It described a five-sided figure."],"It sounded impatient and cutting.","Here peppery refers to irritable, sharp speech.","meaning")]});
D("per",{etymology:E("From Latin per ‘through, by, for each’; in English the preposition marks a rate for each unit or, in formal use, conformity with a rule or authority.",null,"per",null,"Etymonline, per (https://www.etymonline.com/word/per)."),contexts:[C("per.s1","通用","The train travels at ninety kilometers per hour on the straight section of track.","列車在筆直的路段上以每小時九十公里行駛。","Per means for each one and is used to express a rate.","Per hour sets the unit for the rate; at ninety kilometers gives the distance rate.","The speed is measured for each hour of travel."),C("per.s2","正式","Per the safety notice, visitors must wear eye protection inside the workshop.","根據安全公告，訪客在工作坊內必須佩戴護目裝備。","In formal usage, per means according to or in accordance with.","Per introduces the source rule; must wear expresses the requirement.","The notice is the authority for the instruction.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The sign read “No entry per the fire code,” but the guard claimed per meant “contrary to” and let everyone enter.","The sign read “No entry per the fire code,” meaning entry was prohibited according to the fire code.","In formal use per means according to, not contrary to; the sign invokes the code as its authority.")],quiz:[Q("per.q1","per.s1","meaning","In “sixty miles per hour,” per means ___.",["for each","before each","without any"],"for each","The phrase gives a distance for each hour.","meaning"),Q("per.q2","per.s2","context","“Per the written policy, all guests sign in” means ___.",["According to the written policy, guests sign in.","Guests sign in once every written word.","The policy was written after guests signed in."],"According to the written policy, guests sign in.","This formal use of per cites the rule being followed.","context"),Q("per.q3","per.s1","grammar","Which phrase correctly gives a rate for each day?",["three deliveries per day","three deliveries under day","three deliveries despite day"],"three deliveries per day","Per links the amount to its unit of time.","grammar"),Q("per.q4","per.s2","word-choice","____ the manual, disconnect power before opening the case.",["Per","Pepper","Peril"],"Per","Per introduces the manual as the source of the instruction.","word-choice")]});
D("per capita",{etymology:E("A Latin phrase meaning ‘by the head’: per means ‘for each’ and capita is the plural of caput ‘head’; English uses it for a total calculated or allocated for each person.","per","caput",null,"Etymonline, per capita (https://www.etymonline.com/word/per%20capita)."),contexts:[C("per capita.s1","經濟","The city compared annual water use per capita so that neighborhoods of different sizes could be compared fairly.","市府比較每人每年的用水量，讓人口規模不同的社區可以公平比較。","Per capita means calculated by dividing a total by the number of people.","Per capita modifies water use; so that introduces the purpose of the comparison.","Dividing by residents makes the figures comparable across neighborhoods."),C("per capita.s2","經濟","The relief fund allocated one blanket per capita, giving each displaced resident the same share.","救援基金按人分配毯子，讓每位流離失所的居民都得到相同份額。","Per capita can mean for or by each person.","One blanket per capita states the individual allotment; each restates its fairness.","The amount is assigned to every person individually.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The report listed a per capita income of $40,000 for a family of four, meaning each family member earned $160,000.","The report listed a per capita income of $40,000 for a family of four, meaning the average for each person was $40,000.","Per capita divides the total by the number of people; it does not multiply the stated individual average.")],quiz:[Q("per capita.q1","per capita.s1","meaning","A per capita figure is usually calculated ___.",["for each person in the population","for each square kilometer only","once for the whole century"],"for each person in the population","The total is divided by the number of people.","meaning"),Q("per capita.q2","per capita.s2","context","A shelter distributes one meal per capita. How many meals does each resident receive?",["One","Four, regardless of the number of residents","None"],"One","Per capita in this allocation means for each person.","context"),Q("per capita.q3","per capita.s1","word-choice","Researchers divided the town’s waste total by its residents to report waste ____.",["per capita","peppery","penmanship"],"per capita","The rate is calculated for each resident.","word-choice"),Q("per capita.q4","per capita.s2","word-formation","In the Latin phrase per capita, caput means ___.",["head","payment","island"],"head","Capita is the plural of caput, ‘head’, yielding the phrase ‘by the head’.","word-formation")]});
D("perceivable",{etymology:E("Formed from perceive + -able; perceive came through Old French from Latin percipere ‘take in, understand’, and -able makes an adjective meaning capable of being perceived.",null,"perceive","-able","Etymonline, perceive (https://www.etymonline.com/word/perceive)."),contexts:[C("perceivable.s1","通用","With the room silent, a faint vibration became perceivable through the soles of our shoes.","房間安靜下來後，我們的鞋底感覺得到微弱的震動。","Perceivable means capable of being noticed through the senses or mind.","Became perceivable describes the vibration; through the soles specifies how it is sensed.","The vibration is weak but can be detected by touch once background noise stops.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The change was perceivable to nobody, yet every observer clearly noticed it at once.","The change was perceivable to the observers, who clearly noticed it at once.","Perceivable means able to be noticed; saying nobody could perceive it contradicts everyone noticing it.")],quiz:[Q("perceivable.q1","perceivable.s1","meaning","If a difference is perceivable, it is ___.",["capable of being noticed","impossible to detect","already forgotten"],"capable of being noticed","The suffix -able marks possibility: the difference can be perceived.","meaning"),Q("perceivable.q2","perceivable.s1","context","Which change is perceivable by touch?",["A slight tremor under a person’s fingers","A color hidden in a sealed opaque box","A sound in a room with no air movement or listener"],"A slight tremor under a person’s fingers","A person can detect the tremor through touch.","context"),Q("perceivable.q3","perceivable.s1","word-choice","The scent was faint but still ____ near the open jar.",["perceivable","pentagonal","penal"],"perceivable","The faint scent could still be detected.","word-choice"),Q("perceivable.q4","perceivable.s1","word-formation","What does -able add to perceive in perceivable?",["the sense of being capable of being perceived","the sense of occurring in the past","the sense of being a person"],"the sense of being capable of being perceived","The suffix -able forms an adjective expressing capability or possibility.","word-formation")]});
D("perceive",{etymology:E("From Old French perceivre, from Latin percipere ‘take entirely, seize, understand’, formed from per ‘through’ + capere ‘take’; English uses it for sensing and for regarding or understanding.","per","capere",null,"Etymonline, perceive (https://www.etymonline.com/word/perceive)."),contexts:[C("perceive.s1","心理","From the balcony, the guard perceived a faint flash near the service entrance and called the control room.","警衛從陽台察覺服務入口附近有一道微弱閃光，便通知控制室。","To perceive is to become aware of something through the senses or mind.","Perceived takes a flash as object; from the balcony states the observer’s position.","The guard detects a visual signal that is difficult to see."),C("perceive.s2","通用","Many readers perceive the final chapter as a warning rather than a promise of easy success.","許多讀者把最後一章理解為警告，而不是輕易成功的承諾。","To perceive something as a certain way is to understand or regard it in that way.","Perceive takes the chapter as object and as a warning as its interpretation.","The sentence expresses the readers’ interpretation, not a sensory detection.")],mistakes:[M("grammar","Many readers perceive the final chapter like a promise of easy success rather than as a warning.","Many readers perceive the final chapter as a promise of easy success rather than as a warning.","When perceive means regard or interpret, the standard construction is perceive something as something.")],quiz:[Q("perceive.q1","perceive.s1","meaning","To perceive a faint sound is to ___.",["become aware of it by hearing","write it down from memory","make it disappear"],"become aware of it by hearing","This is the sensory-awareness sense of perceive.","meaning"),Q("perceive.q2","perceive.s2","context","If a critic perceives a scene as ironic, the critic ___.",["interprets or regards it as ironic","hears it more loudly than others","changes the scene itself"],"interprets or regards it as ironic","Perceive as expresses an interpretation or point of view.","context"),Q("perceive.q3","perceive.s2","grammar","Complete the usual pattern: “They perceived the remark ____ a joke.”",["as","at","by"],"as","The construction is perceive something as something.","grammar"),Q("perceive.q4","perceive.s1","word-choice","The night watchman could barely ____ movement behind the curtain.",["perceive","pension","pepper"],"perceive","He becomes aware of faint movement through sight.","word-choice")]});
D("percent",{etymology:E("From per cent, a shortening of Latin per centum ‘by the hundred’; it denotes a number or rate out of one hundred.","per","centum",null,"Etymonline, percent (https://www.etymonline.com/word/percent)."),contexts:[C("percent.s1","數學","The survey found that 18 percent of respondents chose the evening class over the morning option.","調查發現，百分之十八的受訪者選擇晚間課程，而非早上的選項。","Percent expresses a number of parts out of one hundred.","Eighteen percent of respondents gives the share; chose states their selection.","The figure means eighteen of every hundred respondents."),C("percent.s2","數學","Only five percent remained after the battery lost most of its charge during the trip.","電池在旅途中失去大部分電量後，只剩下百分之五。","After a number, percent states a rate out of one hundred.","Five percent is the remaining rate; after identifies what reduced it.","The remaining charge is five parts per hundred of the full amount.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The notice says 25 percent of the boxes were damaged, so all 100 boxes were damaged.","The notice says 25 percent of the boxes were damaged, so 25 of every 100 were damaged.","Twenty-five percent is one quarter, not the whole set of 100 boxes.")],quiz:[Q("percent.q1","percent.s1","meaning","What does 25 percent mean?",["25 parts out of every 100","25 parts out of every 10","Every part of the total"],"25 parts out of every 100","Percent is based on one hundred.","meaning"),Q("percent.q2","percent.s2","context","A phone has 40 percent battery remaining. How much of a full charge remains?",["Forty parts out of one hundred","Four times a full charge","No charge at all"],"Forty parts out of one hundred","The percentage states the fraction of the full charge remaining.","context"),Q("percent.q3","percent.s1","word-choice","The price rose by ten ____ after the tax changed.",["percent","perceive","pence"],"percent","The sentence names a proportional rate of increase.","word-choice"),Q("percent.q4","percent.s1","word-formation","The Latin phrase behind percent, per centum, means ___.",["by the hundred","through the head","almost an island"],"by the hundred","Per centum literally means ‘by the hundred’.","word-formation")]});
D("percentage",{etymology:E("Formed from percent + -age; percent comes from Latin per centum ‘by the hundred’, while -age forms a noun for an amount or rate.",null,"percent","-age","Etymonline, percentage (https://www.etymonline.com/word/percentage)."),contexts:[C("percentage.s1","通用","A high percentage of the seedlings survived because the greenhouse kept them warm through the frost.","由於溫室在霜凍期間保持溫暖，很大比例的幼苗存活下來。","A percentage is an amount expressed as a number out of one hundred.","A high percentage of the seedlings is the subject; because gives the reason.","The phrase refers to the share of seedlings that survived, not their raw count.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The survey’s percentage was 42 people, without comparing that count to the total number who answered.","The survey found that 42 percent of respondents chose the option, expressing the share out of one hundred.","A percentage expresses a proportion out of one hundred; a raw count of people alone is not a percentage.")],quiz:[Q("percentage.q1","percentage.s1","meaning","A percentage expresses ___.",["a share as a number out of one hundred","a total number without a denominator","a distance measured in kilometers"],"a share as a number out of one hundred","A percentage states a proportion based on 100.","meaning"),Q("percentage.q2","percentage.s1","context","Which report includes a percentage?",["Thirty percent of the votes were cast early.","Thirty voters arrived before noon.","The ballot box is thirty centimeters wide."],"Thirty percent of the votes were cast early.","Thirty percent states a share out of one hundred.","context"),Q("percentage.q3","percentage.s1","word-choice","The ____ of residents using buses increased from 20% to 27%.",["percentage","perceptive","peninsula"],"percentage","The sentence describes a changing proportion of residents.","word-choice"),Q("percentage.q4","percentage.s1","word-formation","Which element turns percent into the noun percentage?",["-age","-less","-ful"],"-age","The suffix -age forms the noun for a rate or amount here.","word-formation")]});
D("perceptible",{etymology:E("From Latin perceptibilis, from percipere ‘perceive’ + -ibilis; it means capable of being perceived by the senses or otherwise noticed.",null,"percipere","-ible","Etymonline, perceptible (https://www.etymonline.com/word/perceptible)."),contexts:[C("perceptible.s1","通用","There was a perceptible pause before the witness answered the judge’s final question.","證人回答法官最後一個問題前，停頓了一下，這停頓清楚可察。","Perceptible means able to be seen, heard, or otherwise noticed.","Perceptible modifies pause; before marks when it occurred.","The pause was noticeable to observers, although it may have been brief.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The temperature change was perceptible to no instrument or person, yet everyone clearly felt it.","The temperature change was perceptible to everyone, who clearly felt it.","Perceptible means noticeable; claiming nobody could sense it conflicts with everyone feeling it.")],quiz:[Q("perceptible.q1","perceptible.s1","meaning","A perceptible change is one that can be ___.",["noticed","prevented from ever occurring","used as a measurement unit"],"noticed","Perceptible describes something detectable by the senses or mind.","meaning"),Q("perceptible.q2","perceptible.s1","context","Which would be a perceptible pause?",["A brief silence that listeners can hear","An unrecorded thought no one can observe","A color inside a sealed opaque box"],"A brief silence that listeners can hear","Listeners can notice the pause in speech.","context"),Q("perceptible.q3","perceptible.s1","word-choice","The new paint produced a ____ change in the room’s brightness.",["perceptible","pensive","penal"],"perceptible","The brightness change could be noticed.","word-choice"),Q("perceptible.q4","perceptible.s1","meaning","If a scent is perceptible, it is ___.",["detectable by smell","impossible to smell","a person who studies minerals"],"detectable by smell","The adjective applies to something that can be noticed, including by smell.","meaning")]});
D("perception",{etymology:E("From Latin perceptio ‘a receiving, perception’, from percipere ‘take in, understand’; the English noun covers sensory awareness and a person’s understanding or opinion.",null,"percipere","-tion","Etymonline, perception (https://www.etymonline.com/word/perception)."),contexts:[C("perception.s1","心理","Her perception of the room changed when the lights revealed the water stain on the ceiling.","燈光照出天花板上的水漬後，她對房間的觀感改變了。","Perception is the way someone notices things through the senses or an opinion formed about them.","Her perception of the room is the subject; when introduces the new evidence.","The newly visible stain changes how she understands the room.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","His perception of the painting was his physical canvas, wooden frame, and wet oil paint rather than his way of seeing or understanding it.","His perception of the painting was his interpretation of its colors and meaning.","Perception refers to sensory awareness or an interpretation, not the physical object itself.")],quiz:[Q("perception.q1","perception.s1","meaning","A person’s perception is their way of ___.",["noticing or understanding something","repairing a machine","measuring only its weight"],"noticing or understanding something","Perception concerns awareness through the senses or an opinion.","meaning"),Q("perception.q2","perception.s1","context","Why might two viewers have different perceptions of a painting?",["They may interpret its image and meaning differently.","They must be looking at two different planets.","A perception is always an exact measurement."],"They may interpret its image and meaning differently.","Perception can refer to a subjective understanding or opinion.","context"),Q("perception.q3","perception.s1","word-choice","The sudden noise changed her ____ of how safe the empty street felt.",["perception","pentagon","peppermint"],"perception","The sentence describes her changed understanding of the street.","word-choice"),Q("perception.q4","perception.s1","meaning","Which phrase uses perception in the sense of an opinion?",["Public perception of the proposal improved.","The perception contains two wheels.","She perceived the bell by ringing it."],"Public perception of the proposal improved.","Public perception refers to what people think about the proposal.","meaning")]});
D("perceptive",{etymology:E("Formed from perceive + -ive; perceive came from Latin percipere ‘take in, understand’, and -ive makes an adjective describing a person who notices and understands things well.",null,"perceive","-ive","Etymonline, perceptive (https://www.etymonline.com/word/perceptive)."),contexts:[C("perceptive.s1","性格","The perceptive nurse noticed that the patient’s smile did not match his tense hands and asked whether he was worried.","敏銳的護理師注意到病人的笑容與緊握的雙手不相稱，便問他是否擔心。","Perceptive describes someone good at noticing and understanding details.","Perceptive modifies nurse; that introduces the mismatch she notices.","She infers hidden anxiety from nonverbal signs others might overlook.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The perceptive detective overlooked every clue and misunderstood what the witness had plainly said.","The perceptive detective noticed the small clues and understood what the witness had implied.","A perceptive person notices and understands details; overlooking every clue contradicts the adjective.")],quiz:[Q("perceptive.q1","perceptive.s1","meaning","A perceptive listener is good at ___.",["noticing and understanding subtle details","ignoring every part of a conversation","speaking louder than everyone"],"noticing and understanding subtle details","Perceptive means quick to notice and understand things.","meaning"),Q("perceptive.q2","perceptive.s1","context","Which action is perceptive?",["Noticing a colleague is uneasy despite a cheerful answer","Repeating a sentence without hearing it","Forgetting a clear instruction immediately"],"Noticing a colleague is uneasy despite a cheerful answer","The person reads a subtle mismatch in words and mood.","context"),Q("perceptive.q3","perceptive.s1","word-choice","Her ____ comments showed she had spotted the flaw hidden in the proposal.",["perceptive","perishable","pension"],"perceptive","She notices and understands a subtle flaw.","word-choice"),Q("perceptive.q4","perceptive.s1","meaning","Why is the reviewer called perceptive?",["She recognizes the unstated assumption behind the argument.","She cannot follow the argument.","She changes the paper’s font."],"She recognizes the unstated assumption behind the argument.","Seeing an unstated assumption shows keen understanding.","meaning")]});
D("perceptual",{etymology:E("Formed from perception + -al; perception derives from Latin percipere ‘take in, understand’. The adjective usually means relating to sensory awareness and can also describe keen insight.",null,"perception","-al","Etymonline, perceptual (https://www.etymonline.com/word/perceptual)."),contexts:[C("perceptual.s1","通用","The experiment measured perceptual differences in brightness by asking volunteers to compare two gray panels.","這項實驗讓志願者比較兩塊灰色面板，以測量亮度感知上的差異。","Perceptual means relating to the ability to notice things through the senses.","Perceptual modifies differences; by asking explains how the researchers measured them.","Volunteers judge brightness through visual perception."),C("perceptual.s2","通用","Her perceptual reading of the negotiation revealed that the silence signaled hesitation, not agreement.","她敏銳地解讀談判過程，發現沉默表示猶豫，而非同意。","Perceptual can describe an interpretation showing quick understanding of people or situations.","Perceptual modifies reading; that-clause gives the insight she reached.","The speaker infers the other party’s hesitation from the conversational silence.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The perceptual test measured hearing and vision, but the report said perceptual could only describe a person’s shoe size.","The perceptual test measured hearing and vision, using perceptual in its sensory-related sense.","Perceptual relates to sensory awareness; shoe size is not its only or relevant meaning.")],quiz:[Q("perceptual.q1","perceptual.s1","meaning","Perceptual skills involve ___.",["noticing information through the senses","calculating a pension payment","drawing a five-sided figure"],"noticing information through the senses","The common adjective sense concerns sensory awareness.","meaning"),Q("perceptual.q2","perceptual.s2","context","A perceptual reading of a tense meeting might notice ___.",["that a long silence signals hesitation","only the color of the chairs","the exact weight of the table"],"that a long silence signals hesitation","This use describes a keen interpretation of a situation.","context"),Q("perceptual.q3","perceptual.s1","word-choice","The study compared ____ judgments of shape made by people with different vision.",["perceptual","penal","peppery"],"perceptual","The judgments concern how people see and notice shapes.","word-choice"),Q("perceptual.q4","perceptual.s2","meaning","Which comment is perceptual in the keen-insight sense?",["“Her pause suggests she is unsure, despite saying yes.”","“The folder is blue.”","“The clock has a round face.”"],"“Her pause suggests she is unsure, despite saying yes.”","This interpretation reads a subtle human cue.","meaning")]});
