D("periodically",{etymology:E("Formed from periodic + adverb suffix -ally; periodic comes from Greek periodikos ‘recurring at intervals’, based on periodos ‘cycle’.",null,"periodic","-ally","Etymonline, periodic (https://www.etymonline.com/word/periodically)."),contexts:[C("periodically.s1","通用","The pump shuts down periodically every two hours so the filters can be cleaned on schedule.","水泵每兩小時定期停機一次，以便按時清理濾網。","Periodically means happening again at intervals, often on a planned timetable.","Periodically modifies shuts down; every two hours specifies the regular schedule.","The stoppage recurs at fixed intervals."),C("periodically.s2","通用","I still hear from my former teacher periodically, usually when she visits our city.","我仍不時收到以前老師的消息，通常是在她來我們城市時。","Periodically can also mean from time to time without a strict clock.","Periodically modifies hear from; usually adds a loose recurring circumstance.","Contact occurs occasionally, linked to visits rather than a fixed schedule.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The pump ran periodically for exactly one second in its entire lifetime and never repeated the event.","The pump ran once for one second; periodically would mean it ran again at intervals.","Periodically suggests recurrence, either at regular intervals or from time to time.")],quiz:[Q("periodically.q1","periodically.s1","meaning","A sensor that reports periodically every minute reports ___.",["at regular one-minute intervals","only one time ever","at a completely unrelated rate each time"],"at regular one-minute intervals","This sense describes scheduled recurrence.","meaning"),Q("periodically.q2","periodically.s2","context","“She visits periodically” can mean she visits ___.",["from time to time","every exact second","only before she was born"],"from time to time","The looser sense means occasionally, not at an exact interval.","context"),Q("periodically.q3","periodically.s1","word-choice","The filter should be replaced ____ every six months.",["periodically","perceptually","perilously"],"periodically","The replacement recurs on a six-month schedule.","word-choice"),Q("periodically.q4","periodically.s2","meaning","Which sentence best fits the occasional sense?",["We meet periodically when our travels happen to overlap.","The bell rings at exactly 8:00 every day.","The clock ticks every second."],"We meet periodically when our travels happen to overlap.","The meetings happen now and then without a strict timetable.","meaning")]});
D("periodization",{etymology:E("Formed from period + -ize + -ation; period comes through Latin periodus from Greek periodos ‘cycle/course’. Periodization is the act of dividing a subject or history into named periods.",null,"period","-ization","Etymonline, period (https://www.etymonline.com/word/period)."),contexts:[C("periodization.s1","歷史","The course’s periodization divides the empire’s history into founding, expansion, and decline.","課程的時期劃分把帝國史分成建立、擴張和衰落三段。","Periodization is the act of organizing history or another subject into named periods.","Periodization is the subject; into introduces the resulting categories.","The historian uses a framework to segment a long past into stages.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The historian’s periodization refused to divide history into any periods and treated every date as exactly the same stage.","The historian’s periodization organized history into distinct named periods and stages.","Periodization is precisely the act of organizing a subject into periods.")],quiz:[Q("periodization.q1","periodization.s1","meaning","Periodization is the process of ___.",["dividing history or a subject into periods","measuring a shape’s border","publishing a magazine every week"],"dividing history or a subject into periods","The term names a framework of distinct chronological stages.","meaning"),Q("periodization.q2","periodization.s1","context","A historian who labels eras “ancient,” “medieval,” and “modern” is using ___.",["periodization","percussion","permafrost"],"periodization","The labels divide the past into named periods.","context"),Q("periodization.q3","periodization.s1","word-choice","The textbook’s ____ separates the revolution into three stages.",["periodization","periscope","perjury"],"periodization","It organizes the historical event into stages or periods.","word-choice"),Q("periodization.q4","periodization.s1","meaning","Why might scholars disagree about periodization?",["They may draw the boundaries between historical stages differently.","They cannot tell a circle from a line.","The term refers to an instrument for looking underwater."],"They may draw the boundaries between historical stages differently.","Different choices of periods create different historical frameworks.","meaning")]});
D("peripheral",{etymology:E("From Greek peripherikos ‘around the circumference’, from peripherein ‘carry around’, based on peri ‘around’; English means at an outer edge and, figuratively, not central to a topic.","peri","pherein","-al","Etymonline, peripheral (https://www.etymonline.com/word/peripheral)."),contexts:[C("peripheral.s1","通用","The trail passes through the peripheral villages before reaching the region’s central market town.","小徑先經過外圍村莊，才抵達該區的中心市鎮。","Peripheral means located at an edge rather than at the center.","Peripheral modifies villages; before marks their position on the route.","The villages lie outside the region’s central settlement."),C("peripheral.s2","通用","The color of the folder was peripheral to the investigation, which focused on who had altered the figures.","資料夾的顏色與調查重點無關，調查關注的是誰修改了數字。","Peripheral can mean not central to the main question or purpose.","Peripheral to links the detail to the investigation; which explains its actual focus.","Folder color does not affect the central issue of altered data.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The peripheral issue was the main question that decided the investigation, while the altered records were irrelevant.","The central issue was the altered records; the folder’s color was peripheral to the investigation.","Peripheral in the figurative sense means noncentral, the opposite of the main question.")],quiz:[Q("peripheral.q1","peripheral.s1","meaning","A peripheral road runs ___.",["around the outer edge","through the exact center only","under the ocean floor"],"around the outer edge","The spatial sense means located at the edge rather than the center.","meaning"),Q("peripheral.q2","peripheral.s2","context","Which detail is peripheral to a study of air quality?",["The color of the researcher’s notebook","The amount of pollution measured","The location of the air sensors"],"The color of the researcher’s notebook","Notebook color does not bear on the study’s main question.","context"),Q("peripheral.q3","peripheral.s1","word-choice","The town built a ____ road around the edge of the old center.",["peripheral","perilous","perceptive"],"peripheral","The road is located around the outer boundary.","word-choice"),Q("peripheral.q4","peripheral.s2","meaning","If a concern is peripheral to a decision, it is ___.",["not central to the main issue","the only decisive factor","the decision’s final result"],"not central to the main issue","The figurative sense means secondary or nonessential to the main point.","meaning")]});
D("peripherally",{etymology:E("Formed from peripheral + adverb suffix -ly; peripheral comes from Greek peripherikos ‘around the circumference’ and developed a figurative sense ‘not central’.",null,"peripheral","-ly","Etymonline, peripheral (https://www.etymonline.com/word/peripherally)."),contexts:[C("peripherally.s1","通用","The camera recorded the crowd peripherally, catching movement at the edge of the frame rather than the main speaker.","攝影機從邊緣拍到人群的動態，沒有聚焦在主講者身上。","Peripherally means at an outer edge or in a way that is not central to the main point.","Peripherally modifies recorded; rather than contrasts the edge with the central subject.","The crowd appears near the frame’s boundary, outside the central focus.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The report discussed the budget peripherally by making it the sole topic of every section and ignoring all other matters.","The report discussed the budget centrally by making it the sole topic of every section.","Peripherally means on the edge or not central; a sole, repeated focus is central.")],quiz:[Q("peripherally.q1","peripherally.s1","meaning","To see something peripherally is to see it ___.",["near the edge of one’s field of view","directly at the center of focus only","after closing one’s eyes"],"near the edge of one’s field of view","The adverb retains the outer-edge meaning.","meaning"),Q("peripherally.q2","peripherally.s1","context","A report mentions a side issue only peripherally. How does it treat it?",["As a minor point rather than the main focus","As the only subject throughout","As the final conclusion"],"As a minor point rather than the main focus","The figurative adverb means in a noncentral way.","context"),Q("peripherally.q3","peripherally.s1","word-choice","The passing cyclist appeared ____ at the edge of the photograph.",["peripherally","periodically","perilously"],"peripherally","The cyclist was at the image’s outer edge.","word-choice"),Q("peripherally.q4","peripherally.s1","meaning","What is a peripheral mention of cost?",["A brief side note, not the main discussion","A detailed section devoted entirely to cost","A receipt proving the exact amount"],"A brief side note, not the main discussion","The adverb can mean in a secondary or noncentral way.","meaning")]});
D("periphery",{etymology:E("From Latin peripheria and Greek periphereia ‘circumference’, from peripherein ‘carry around’; English names the outer edge of an area.","peri","pherein","-y","Etymonline, periphery (https://www.etymonline.com/word/periphery)."),contexts:[C("periphery.s1","地理","Small farms dotted the periphery of the city, beyond the dense apartment blocks and shopping streets.","小農場散布在城市外圍，遠離密集公寓和商業街。","The periphery is the outer edge of an area.","The periphery is the object of dotted; beyond contrasts it with the dense center.","The farms lie at the city’s outer boundary.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The periphery of the circle was its central point, exactly halfway from every edge.","The center of the circle was its central point; the periphery was the outer edge.","Periphery means the outer edge, not the center.")],quiz:[Q("periphery.q1","periphery.s1","meaning","The periphery of a town is its ___.",["outer edge","main square only","deepest underground level"],"outer edge","The noun names the outer boundary of an area.","meaning"),Q("periphery.q2","periphery.s1","context","Where might new warehouses be built if they are on the city’s periphery?",["Near the city’s outer edge","In the exact center of the old market","Far below street level"],"Near the city’s outer edge","Periphery refers to the outer part of the city.","context"),Q("periphery.q3","periphery.s1","word-choice","A ring road follows the ____ of the metropolitan area.",["periphery","perfection","percussion"],"periphery","The road follows the area’s outer edge.","word-choice"),Q("periphery.q4","periphery.s1","meaning","Which is closest in meaning to periphery?",["border or outer edge","central point","interior room"],"border or outer edge","The periphery is the boundary around an area.","meaning")]});
D("periscope",{etymology:E("Formed from Greek peri ‘around’ + skopein ‘look at’; coined for an optical instrument that lets someone see over or around an obstruction, notably from a submarine.","peri","skopein","-scope","Etymonline, periscope (https://www.etymonline.com/word/periscope)."),contexts:[C("periscope.s1","航海","From below the waterline, the submarine commander raised the periscope to check for ships on the horizon.","潛艇指揮官在水線下升起潛望鏡，查看地平線上的船隻。","A periscope is an optical tube that lets a viewer see objects outside the direct line of sight.","Raised the periscope states the action; to check gives its purpose.","The instrument carries a view from the hidden submarine to the surface.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The submarine commander used a periscope to see through solid steel walls without mirrors, lenses, or any optical path.","The submarine commander used a periscope to view ships above the water through its optical path.","A periscope uses an optical arrangement to redirect a view; it does not see through solid walls magically.")],quiz:[Q("periscope.q1","periscope.s1","meaning","A periscope helps someone ___.",["see around or over an obstruction","hear through a wall","measure a boundary’s length"],"see around or over an obstruction","The instrument redirects a line of sight to an otherwise hidden view.","meaning"),Q("periscope.q2","periscope.s1","context","Why might a submarine raise a periscope?",["To look for ships while remaining below the surface","To drill a hole in the ocean floor","To measure the submarine’s speed"],"To look for ships while remaining below the surface","The optical tube lets the crew view objects above water.","context"),Q("periscope.q3","periscope.s1","word-choice","The sailor looked above the wall through a ____.",["periscope","perjury","perennial"],"periscope","The device allows a view over an obstruction.","word-choice"),Q("periscope.q4","periscope.s1","word-formation","The element -scope in periscope is associated with ___.",["looking or viewing","freezing ground","a regular payment"],"looking or viewing","Greek skopein means ‘look at’, the source of -scope.","word-formation")]});
D("perish",{etymology:E("From Old French perir ‘be lost, die’, from Latin perire ‘pass away, be destroyed’, from per ‘through’ + ire ‘go’; English has senses of death, destruction, and decay.","per","ire",null,"Etymonline, perish (https://www.etymonline.com/word/perish)."),contexts:[C("perish.s1","書面","Several sailors perished when the small vessel capsized in the freezing night sea.","小船在寒冷的夜海中翻覆時，幾名水手喪生。","To perish is to die, especially suddenly or violently.","Perished is the main verb; when introduces the fatal event.","The sailors die in a sudden maritime disaster."),C("perish.s2","書面","Without public support, the fragile language may perish within a generation.","若沒有公眾支持，這種脆弱的語言可能在一代之內消亡。","To perish can mean be destroyed or disappear completely.","May perish expresses a possible future; within gives the time limit.","The language could cease to be spoken and disappear."),C("perish.s3","通用","The rubber seal began to perish after years in direct sunlight, becoming brittle and cracked.","橡膠密封圈在陽光直射多年後開始老化，變得脆裂。","Materials or food can perish by decaying or becoming weak and cracked with age.","Began to perish is followed by the result; after gives the exposure period.","The aged rubber deteriorates physically rather than dying as a living creature.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The rubber seal perished in sunlight by becoming stronger, flexible, and completely unchanged after decades.","The rubber seal perished in sunlight by becoming weak, brittle, and cracked after decades.","For rubber, perish means decay or deteriorate, not become stronger and unchanged.")],quiz:[Q("perish.q1","perish.s1","meaning","If sailors perish in a wreck, they ___.",["die","receive a promotion","arrive safely"],"die","This sense means die, often in a disaster.","meaning"),Q("perish.q2","perish.s2","context","A language may perish if ___.",["it disappears and is no longer spoken","it gains new speakers","it is written in a new alphabet"],"it disappears and is no longer spoken","The figurative sense means disappear completely.","context"),Q("perish.q3","perish.s3","meaning","When an old rubber seal perishes, it may ___.",["become brittle and cracked","grow new leaves","turn into a living animal"],"become brittle and cracked","Materials can perish by deteriorating with age.","meaning"),Q("perish.q4","perish.s1","word-choice","Many plants will ____ if they are left without water for too long.",["perish","perceive","percolate"],"perish","Without water, the plants may die.","word-choice")]});
D("perishable",{etymology:E("From perish + -able; perish came from Old French perir and Latin perire ‘pass away, be destroyed’, while -able marks susceptibility, so perishable goods can spoil or decay.",null,"perish","-able","Etymonline, perishable (https://www.etymonline.com/word/perishable)."),contexts:[C("perishable.s1","通用","The market stored perishable berries in a chilled room so they would not spoil before delivery.","市場把易腐的莓果存放在冷藏室，避免它們在送貨前變質。","Perishable describes something likely to rot, spoil, or fade within a short time.","Perishable modifies berries; so introduces the purpose of chilling them.","Cold storage slows the berries’ deterioration."),C("perishable.s2","通用","At the border, officers directed travelers to declare any perishable they were carrying, such as fresh cheese.","在邊境，官員要求旅客申報所攜帶的易腐物品，例如鮮乳酪。","A perishable can be a product, especially food, that goes bad quickly.","A perishable is the object of declare; such as gives an example.","The noun refers to a quickly spoiling item of food.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","Fresh milk is nonperishable and can safely sit unrefrigerated for years without changing.","Fresh milk is perishable and must be stored appropriately to slow spoilage.","Fresh milk spoils; it is a perishable product, not something that remains safe for years at room temperature.")],quiz:[Q("perishable.q1","perishable.s1","meaning","Perishable food is food that ___.",["can spoil or rot relatively quickly","never changes over time","must be frozen solid before it exists"],"can spoil or rot relatively quickly","The adjective marks susceptibility to spoilage.","meaning"),Q("perishable.q2","perishable.s2","context","Which item might a traveler declare as a perishable?",["Fresh cheese","A stainless-steel spoon","A ceramic plate"],"Fresh cheese","Fresh cheese can spoil and is a perishable food product.","context"),Q("perishable.q3","perishable.s1","word-choice","The grocer moved the ____ fruit into refrigeration.",["perishable","perceptive","perennial"],"perishable","Fruit that may spoil is perishable and needs cooling.","word-choice"),Q("perishable.q4","perishable.s2","meaning","In “pack the perishables first,” perishables means ___.",["items, especially foods, that spoil quickly","durable metal tools","paper punctuation marks"],"items, especially foods, that spoil quickly","The noun refers to products liable to go bad soon.","meaning")]});
D("perjury",{etymology:E("From Latin perjurium ‘false oath, perjury’, from perjurare ‘swear falsely’, formed from per ‘thoroughly’ + jurare ‘swear’; the legal offense is lying under oath.","per","jurare","-y","Etymonline, perjury (https://www.etymonline.com/word/perjury)."),contexts:[C("perjury.s1","法律","The witness faced a perjury charge after investigators proved that he knowingly lied under oath about the payment.","調查人員證明證人明知故犯地在宣誓後謊報款項，他因此面臨偽證指控。","Perjury is the offense of lying while under oath in a legal hearing.","A perjury charge is the object; after introduces the evidence behind it.","The witness made a deliberate false statement after swearing to tell the truth.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The witness committed perjury by telling the truth under oath, exactly matching every fact in the record.","The witness avoided perjury by telling the truth under oath, exactly matching every fact in the record.","Perjury requires a false statement under oath; truthful testimony is not perjury.")],quiz:[Q("perjury.q1","perjury.s1","meaning","Perjury is ___.",["knowingly lying under oath in a legal proceeding","forgetting a word in a casual chat","making a lawful payment"],"knowingly lying under oath in a legal proceeding","The offense concerns a false statement made under oath.","meaning"),Q("perjury.q2","perjury.s1","context","Which action could lead to a perjury charge?",["A witness knowingly gives false testimony under oath.","A juror takes notes during a trial.","A visitor arrives late to the courthouse."],"A witness knowingly gives false testimony under oath.","A false sworn statement fits the legal offense.","context"),Q("perjury.q3","perjury.s1","word-choice","The court investigated whether the witness had committed ____.",["perjury","permafrost","percussion"],"perjury","The investigation concerns a possible lie under oath.","word-choice"),Q("perjury.q4","perjury.s1","meaning","Why is an oath relevant to perjury?",["The offense involves lying after swearing to tell the truth.","An oath is a type of courtroom furniture.","Perjury means missing a scheduled class."],"The offense involves lying after swearing to tell the truth.","The sworn setting distinguishes perjury from an ordinary lie.","meaning")]});
D("perm",{etymology:E("A clipping of permanent wave, originally a chemically or thermally set wave designed to last; as a verb, perm means give hair this lasting curl, and as a noun it names the hairstyle.",null,"permanent wave",null,"Etymonline, perm (https://www.etymonline.com/word/perm)."),contexts:[C("perm.s1","生活","The stylist will perm her straight hair with large rollers to create loose curls that last for months.","髮型師會用大捲筒為她的直髮燙髮，做出可維持數月的鬆捲。","To perm hair is to treat it with chemicals or heat so that it stays curly.","Perm is a transitive verb with hair as object; to create gives the aim.","The treatment changes the hair into a lasting curl pattern."),C("perm.s2","生活","Her new perm looked softer after the first wash, with broad curls instead of tight ringlets.","她的新燙髮第一次洗過後看起來更柔和，呈現大捲而不是緊密的小卷。","A perm is a hairstyle of curls set by a permanent wave treatment.","Perm is the subject of looked; after the first wash marks the time.","The noun describes the resulting curled hairstyle.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","She got a perm by cutting off every curl and leaving her hair completely straight, with no chemical or heat treatment.","She got a perm by treating her hair with chemicals or heat to create lasting curls.","A perm creates curls that last; simply cutting curls off to leave straight hair is not a perm.")],quiz:[Q("perm.q1","perm.s1","meaning","To perm someone’s hair is to ___.",["treat it so curls last","shave it completely","wash it with cold water only"],"treat it so curls last","The verb describes a lasting curl treatment.","meaning"),Q("perm.q2","perm.s2","context","A stylist admires a client’s new perm. What are they discussing?",["The client’s set curly hairstyle","A monthly pension payment","A school class period"],"The client’s set curly hairstyle","The noun perm names the resulting curled hairdo.","context"),Q("perm.q3","perm.s1","word-choice","She booked an appointment to ____ her naturally straight hair.",["perm","perish","perceive"],"perm","The stylist will create curls that remain in the hair.","word-choice"),Q("perm.q4","perm.s2","meaning","Why might a perm still show curls after washing?",["The treatment sets a lasting wave pattern.","The hairstyle is a punctuation mark.","The hair is permanently wet."],"The treatment sets a lasting wave pattern.","Perm is clipped from permanent wave and names curls intended to last.","meaning")]});
D("permafrost",{etymology:E("A twentieth-century compound of permanent + frost, coined for ground that remains frozen through summer; the scientific definition generally requires ground at or below 0°C for at least two consecutive years.",null,"permanent + frost",null,"Etymonline, permafrost (https://www.etymonline.com/word/permafrost)."),contexts:[C("permafrost.s1","地理","Road builders drove insulated piles into the permafrost to keep the thawing ground from shifting beneath the highway.","道路施工人員把隔熱樁打入永久凍土，避免融化的地面在公路下移動。","Permafrost is ground that remains at or below freezing through summer as well as winter.","Into the permafrost gives the pile location; to keep states the engineering purpose.","The frozen ground persists across seasons, although warming can destabilize it.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","Permafrost is soil that freezes for one cold night and thaws completely by breakfast each morning.","Permafrost is ground that remains frozen through summer as well as winter for years.","The prefix perma- and the technical definition indicate long-lasting frozen ground, not a nightly freeze.")],quiz:[Q("permafrost.q1","permafrost.s1","meaning","Permafrost is ground that ___.",["stays frozen through warm as well as cold seasons","freezes only for a few hours each night","is permanently covered by liquid water"],"stays frozen through warm as well as cold seasons","The defining point is that the ground remains frozen through summer.","meaning"),Q("permafrost.q2","permafrost.s1","context","Where are engineers likely to account for permafrost?",["In a region where the ground stays frozen for years","On a tropical beach with warm soil","Inside a heated kitchen"],"In a region where the ground stays frozen for years","Permafrost is persistent frozen ground, common in very cold regions.","context"),Q("permafrost.q3","permafrost.s1","word-choice","The northern road’s foundation must be designed for ____ beneath the soil.",["permafrost","perjury","perfection"],"permafrost","Long-term frozen ground can affect foundations.","word-choice"),Q("permafrost.q4","permafrost.s1","meaning","Why can thawing permafrost damage roads?",["Ground that was frozen can shift as it warms.","It makes the road’s perimeter shorter.","It turns every road into a periodical."],"Ground that was frozen can shift as it warms.","When permanently frozen ground thaws, it can lose stability and move.","meaning")]});
D("permanence",{etymology:E("From Latin permanentia, from permanere ‘remain to the end’, formed from per ‘through’ + manere ‘remain’; -ence makes the noun for lasting or enduring.","per","manere","-ence","Etymonline, permanence (https://www.etymonline.com/word/permanence)."),contexts:[C("permanence.s1","通用","The stone inscription gave the memorial a sense of permanence that the temporary banners could not provide.","石刻銘文讓紀念碑具有臨時布條無法提供的持久感。","Permanence is the state of lasting a long time or forever.","A sense of permanence is the object; that-clause contrasts it with temporary banners.","Stone appears enduring compared with decorations that will soon be removed.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The paper sign’s permanence meant it disappeared after one afternoon and could not last beyond the event.","The paper sign’s temporary nature meant it disappeared after one afternoon; permanence would mean lasting much longer.","Permanence is endurance, the opposite of disappearing after a few hours.")],quiz:[Q("permanence.q1","permanence.s1","meaning","Permanence is the quality of ___.",["lasting over time","changing every second","being difficult to see"],"lasting over time","The noun describes a lasting or enduring state.","meaning"),Q("permanence.q2","permanence.s1","context","Which material suggests permanence for an outdoor memorial?",["Engraved stone","A paper banner expected to tear","A soap bubble"],"Engraved stone","Stone can endure much longer than the temporary alternatives.","context"),Q("permanence.q3","permanence.s1","word-choice","The archive seeks the ____ of records that should last for generations.",["permanence","periphery","peril"],"permanence","The archive wants its records to endure.","word-choice"),Q("permanence.q4","permanence.s1","meaning","What contrasts with permanence?",["temporary existence","lasting continuity","enduring presence"],"temporary existence","Temporary existence does not last, the opposite of permanence.","meaning")]});
D("permanent",{etymology:E("From Latin permanentem, present participle of permanere ‘remain to the end’, from per ‘through’ + manere ‘remain’; it describes something lasting or fixed in place/status.","per","manere","-ent","Etymonline, permanent (https://www.etymonline.com/word/permanent)."),contexts:[C("permanent.s1","通用","The museum installed a permanent exhibit on local shipbuilding rather than removing it after the summer.","博物館設置了地方造船史的常設展，而不是在夏天後撤下。","Permanent means lasting for a long time or indefinitely, not temporary.","Permanent modifies exhibit; rather than contrasts it with a temporary display.","The exhibit remains on view beyond one season."),C("permanent.s2","通用","A permanent desk near the window was assigned to the new archivist, who no longer had to reserve space daily.","靠窗的固定辦公桌分配給新檔案管理員，他不必每天再預約座位。","Permanent can mean fixed in place or status rather than changing.","Permanent modifies desk; who introduces the user’s benefit.","The desk assignment stays in the same place rather than rotating.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The gallery’s permanent exhibit was removed after one evening and replaced the next morning, so it was temporary.","The gallery’s temporary exhibit was removed after one evening; a permanent exhibit remains for a long time.","Permanent describes something lasting, not a display removed the same night.")],quiz:[Q("permanent.q1","permanent.s1","meaning","A permanent change is ___.",["intended to last rather than be temporary","scheduled to end in one minute","impossible to notice"],"intended to last rather than be temporary","Permanent contrasts with temporary.","meaning"),Q("permanent.q2","permanent.s2","context","A permanent address is one that ___.",["is the person’s fixed address","changes every hour","is used only for a single letter"],"is the person’s fixed address","This sense is stable rather than changing place or status.","context"),Q("permanent.q3","permanent.s1","word-choice","The city made the mural a ____ feature of the station instead of a one-week display.",["permanent","perilous","periodic"],"permanent","The mural will remain rather than be removed after a week.","word-choice"),Q("permanent.q4","permanent.s2","meaning","Why is a fixed desk called permanent?",["It stays assigned in one place.","It is replaced every day.","It is published at regular intervals."],"It stays assigned in one place.","The second sense describes a stable location or status.","meaning")]});
D("permanently",{etymology:E("Formed from permanent + adverb suffix -ly; permanent comes from Latin permanentem, from permanere ‘remain to the end’.",null,"permanent","-ly","Etymonline, permanent (https://www.etymonline.com/word/permanently)."),contexts:[C("permanently.s1","通用","After the bridge inspection failed, the town permanently closed the crossing and built a replacement upstream.","橋梁檢查未通過後，鎮上永久封閉了這座橋，並在上游另建一座。","Permanently means for all time or for the foreseeable future rather than temporarily.","Permanently modifies closed; after gives the cause and and states the alternative.","The crossing is not merely shut for repairs; it will not reopen.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The library permanently closed for ten minutes on Tuesday and reopened immediately, with no lasting change.","The library temporarily closed for ten minutes on Tuesday and reopened immediately.","A short closure followed by reopening is temporary, not permanent.")],quiz:[Q("permanently.q1","permanently.s1","meaning","If a door is permanently sealed, it is sealed ___.",["for the long term, not temporarily","for one second only","at regular hourly intervals"],"for the long term, not temporarily","The adverb means lasting indefinitely or for the foreseeable future.","meaning"),Q("permanently.q2","permanently.s1","context","Which event happened permanently?",["A factory shut down and will not reopen","A shop closed for lunch and opened again","A gate was locked for one minute"],"A factory shut down and will not reopen","The closure is lasting rather than temporary.","context"),Q("permanently.q3","permanently.s1","word-choice","The flood ____ damaged the old bridge, so it had to be replaced.",["permanently","periodically","peripherally"],"permanently","The damage lasted and required a replacement.","word-choice"),Q("permanently.q4","permanently.s1","meaning","What does permanently add to “moved”?",["The move is lasting rather than temporary.","The move happens once each hour.","The move is only a side issue."],"The move is lasting rather than temporary.","The adverb describes an enduring change.","meaning")]});
D("permeability",{etymology:E("From permeable + -ity; permeable comes from Latin permeare ‘pass through’, formed from per ‘through’ + meare ‘go’. The noun names ease of passage through a material and, in physics, magnetic response.","per","meare","-ity","Etymonline, permeable (https://www.etymonline.com/word/permeable)."),contexts:[C("permeability.s1","科學","The engineer tested the soil’s permeability by measuring how quickly water passed through the compacted sample.","工程師測量水通過壓實土樣的速度，以檢驗土壤的滲透性。","Permeability is how readily liquid or gas can pass through a material.","Permeability is the object of tested; by measuring explains the method.","A rapid flow indicates that the soil lets water pass more easily."),C("permeability.s2","物理","The lab compared the magnetic permeability of two alloys to see which one concentrated the field more effectively.","實驗室比較兩種合金的磁導率，查看哪一種更有效地集中磁場。","Magnetic permeability measures how easily a magnetic field forms in a material.","Magnetic modifies permeability; to see introduces the experiment’s purpose.","The material’s response to a magnetic field is being compared, not fluid flow.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The soil’s permeability was low, so water passed through it instantly without resistance or delay.","The soil’s permeability was high, so water passed through it quickly; low permeability would slow the flow.","High permeability allows easier passage; low permeability means water moves through less readily.")],quiz:[Q("permeability.q1","permeability.s1","meaning","High soil permeability means water can ___.",["pass through the soil readily","never enter the soil","turn into metal"],"pass through the soil readily","This sense measures how easily fluid passes through a material.","meaning"),Q("permeability.q2","permeability.s2","context","A physicist measuring magnetic permeability studies how a material ___.",["responds to a magnetic field","lets rainwater drain through it","resists being cut with scissors"],"responds to a magnetic field","Magnetic permeability concerns formation of a magnetic field in material.","context"),Q("permeability.q3","permeability.s1","word-choice","The porous rock has high water ____ and drains quickly.",["permeability","perjury","perfection"],"permeability","The rock lets water pass through readily.","word-choice"),Q("permeability.q4","permeability.s2","meaning","Which use of permeability is about magnetism rather than fluid?",["The alloy’s magnetic permeability was measured.","The membrane’s water permeability was tested.","The soil’s drainage rate was recorded."],"The alloy’s magnetic permeability was measured.","The magnetic adjective selects the physics sense.","meaning")]});
